      "First Report, Sent Late",
      "I waited for confirmation because I was afraid to be wrong first. Delay increased projected casualties. Fear is not exculpatory, but it is the missing variable.",
      "Exacting Keeper — numerical confession, responsibility without self-dramatizing",
      worldChoice("Raise the bell by hand", "strength", "The first signal sounds across an empty line."),
      worldChoice("Repair the delayed trigger", "agility", "The next warning will not depend on one frightened watcher."),
      "Outpost One Bell Tongue"),
    worldSite("L", "Outpost 2", "north", 25, 13, "ruin",
      "A message station between North and Holy Forest was abandoned when its unit violated orders to escort civilians.",
      "Every bunk is unmade. A civilian-sized cloak sits folded at the foot of each one.",
      "Charge of Abandonment",
      "The unit vacated its post. The attached casualty table records forty-one civilians delivered and zero soldiers returned. The charge is accurate. So is the purpose they served.",
      "Patient Mediator — competing truths placed beside one another",
      worldChoice("Ask Outpost Three for help restoring the beacon", "defense", "Shared labor costs pride and preserves supplies."),
      worldChoice("Spend your own stores to finish it", "strength", "You make the light alone and feel what that choice consumes."),
      "Outpost Two Beacon Lens"),
    worldSite("M", "The Confederation (North)", "north", 17, 11, "ruin",
      "Council halls, guild rooms, a granary, gallery, and collapsed delegate quarters reveal unity as an argument maintained by repeated compromise.",
      "Seat cushions bear repairs in a dozen fabrics. No delegate ever agreed on a color, so they agreed to keep mending all of them.",
      "Blank Delegate Token",
      "Reserved for a participant not yet recognized by charter. A union that knows every future member in advance is only a closed room with a large name.",
      "Patient Mediator — procedural hope, disagreement treated as work",
      worldChoice("Reserve the token for an outsider", "defense", "The future council leaves a place for someone it cannot define yet."),
      worldChoice("Return it to the living settlements", "agility", "Recognition becomes their argument instead of your decree."),
      "Blank Confederation Seat"),
    worldSite("O", "Outpost 3", "north", 33, 10, "town",
      "Sella's home is a living settlement of market, schoolyard, church, lake, adventurers' post, and signal square.",
      "Children compete to guess which distant bell will answer next. Their rules change every time somebody loses.",
      "Sella's Failed Lamp",
      "The lamp has never held magic for more than a breath. Sella keeps it because failure measured carefully is still information—and because she likes the glass.",
      "Restless Builder — quick notes, revisions layered over embarrassment",
      worldChoice("Connect the bell chain", "strength", "Market reports begin moving between living settlements."),
      worldChoice("Teach the children Mera's route signs", "agility", "The map becomes knowledge that outlives its courier."),
      "Sella's Clouded Lamp"),
    worldSite("P", "Serenity", "north", 36, 7, "ruin",
      "Pilgrims practiced cooling anger here before entering the Holy Forest. Quarrel booths preserve petty grievances beside acts of difficult reconciliation.",
      "One wall reads: HE CHEWS LIKE A BESIEGED GATE. Under it: I STILL CHOOSE BREAKFAST WITH HIM. A low, delighted laugh passes through the empty room.",
      "Shrine of the Tired Moonmaiden",
      "She was an exhausted mother who asked the Moon for one more mile. The eclipse found her. She carried twelve children, none her own, and afterward returned to complain about her knees.",
      "Devotional Interpreter — reverent about courage, irreverent about sainthood",
      worldChoice("Preserve the petty quarrels", "resistance", "History keeps the small irritations that made devotion real."),
      worldChoice("Open the booths to new travelers", "defense", "Serenity becomes a practice again instead of a sealed virtue."),
      "Reconciliation Chalk"),

    worldSite("R", "The Confederation (Central)", "central", 17, 13, "ruin",
      "Command halls, census courts, archives, galleries, and an emergency chamber show officials receiving accurate collapse reports while publishing reassurance.",
      "The public gallery floor has a groove where petitioners waited. The private lift beside it reaches the same chamber without passing the line.",
      "Summary for Public Stability",
      "Replace 'uncontrolled flight' with 'temporary redistribution.' Exact field reports remain attached beneath the cover, proving the institution knew what its language concealed.",
      "Exacting Keeper — disciplined clerkly prose, moral fracture visible only in retained attachments",
      worldChoice("Preserve the civic templates without emergency powers", "defense", "Useful order survives after its unanswerable authority is removed."),
      worldChoice("Publish every field report beside its summary", "resistance", "Reassurance loses the privilege of hiding its evidence."),
      "Redacted Census Ribbon"),
    worldSite("X", "Luvare", "central", 14, 24, "ruin",
      "Armor baths, laundries, mortuary rooms, pumps, and confession niches cleaned what victory speeches left on returning soldiers.",
      "Two brothers once scrubbed each other's armor here after their first lost campaign. Neither said the word afraid. Both understood it.",
      "Washer's Return Tally",
