      "Succurrere Relief Seal"),
    worldSite("Z", "Auxilia", "central", 14, 20, "ruin",
      "Ropewalks, cobblers, ration packers, fletchers, and cart yards kept armies moving while remaining absent from heroic histories.",
      "A cobbler hid love notes beneath officers' insoles. Most were never found because the boots' owners did not survive long enough to need repairs.",
      "Sabotaged Departure Manifest",
      "Support workers moved injured soldiers to the wrong columns so they would miss the Spear Offensive. The error rate is too patterned to be accidental.",
      "Restless Builder — technical annotations that turn into coordinated refusal",
      worldChoice("Finish the abandoned supply cart", "strength", "Craft becomes a route to the living instead of another campaign."),
      worldChoice("Teach the manifest trick", "agility", "A bureaucratic weapon changes hands."),
      "Auxilia Blue Cord"),
    worldSite("AA", "Amicitia", "central", 14, 16, "ruin",
      "Diplomatic homes and favor ledgers preserve a marriage whose third signature made political duty into a language of love.",
      "One couple maintained separate teacups for formal quarrels and drank from the chipped red pair whenever they had already forgiven each other.",
      "The Third Signature",
      "The spouses signed, then their rival signed as witness because only somebody who had opposed them could certify that neither had been coerced.",
      "Patient Mediator — affectionate precision, rivalry treated as accountable intimacy",
      worldChoice("Return the signet before using it", "defense", "A family's claim takes priority over your access."),
      worldChoice("Open the archive, then return it openly", "agility", "You accept benefit and preserve a trail others can judge."),
      "Amicitia Foreign Signet"),
    worldSite("AB", "Salus", "central", 18, 16, "ruin",
      "Hospital wards, plague gates, herb gardens, and shelters record Askers failing as the world became unable—not unwilling—to answer.",
      "A surgeon's favorite spoon is tied to a medicine cabinet. Somebody stole every useful instrument except the ridiculous spoon.",
      "Clinic Request Log",
      "The world heard her. I felt it turn toward the child. Nothing followed. Love remained; capacity did not. We used boiled thread and our hands.",
      "Practical Caretaker — clinical method interrupted by one unbearable metaphysical observation",
      worldChoice("Treat the survivor with ordinary medicine", "resistance", "Mundane care succeeds without waiting for a miracle."),
      worldChoice("Replant the herb beds", "defense", "A future clinic begins with slow, fallible growth."),
      "Salus Boiled-Thread Kit"),
    worldSite("AC", "Adiuvare", "central", 22, 16, "ruin",
      "Canal locks, bridge shops, road ledgers, and crew housing center on a bridge designed to come apart so civilians could escape.",
      "Every crew member painted one hidden fish beneath the bridge. None are anatomically convincing.",
      "Dismantling Specification",
      "Civil release requires six pins removed in reverse order. Later officials classified the successful escape as sabotage because the bridge did not remain useful to command.",
      "Restless Builder — proud engineering notes, jokes embedded in tolerances",
      worldChoice("Repair the canal toward Foederati", "strength", "Water and people gain a route the old command cannot close."),
      worldChoice("Preserve the removable design", "agility", "The rebuilt route keeps an escape inside its structure."),
      "Adiuvare Release Pin"),
    worldSite("AD", "Auxilium", "central", 26, 16, "ruin",
      "Emergency warehouses achieved mathematically perfect allocations while one sealed room spoiled in untouched excess.",
      "A rat nest contains ration labels from districts officially reported as fully supplied.",
      "Allocation Proof",
      "Every authorized category received its percentage. People outside the categories received zero. The totals reconcile perfectly with a disaster.",
      "Exacting Keeper — flawless arithmetic, no permission to question definitions",
      worldChoice("Distribute supplies now", "defense", "Immediate need outweighs the elegance of a future reserve."),
      worldChoice("Reserve a transparent emergency share", "resistance", "You keep provisions while making the criteria revisable."),
      "Auxilium Brass Measure"),
    worldSite("AE", "Defensor Fidei", "central", 30, 16, "ruin",
      "Sun temples, courts, punishment rooms, and an appeal stair preserve justice powerful enough to confront commanders and rigid enough to erase circumstance.",
      "The appeal stair is lower in the middle where generations stood arguing that the law had misunderstood their lives.",
      "Child v. Commander",
      "The child prevailed because the Sun's law admitted no rank above testimony. The next file reaches a tidy verdict by removing everything that made a different child afraid.",
      "Devotional Interpreter — reverent case commentary willing to record divine law's wound",
      worldChoice("Restore the public appeal stair", "strength", "The court's most important architecture becomes usable again."),
      worldChoice("Pair every verdict with its circumstances", "agility", "Law remains legible but loses the fiction of identical lives."),
      "Sun Court Appeal Chip"),
    worldSite("AF", "Barbarus", "central", 34, 20, "ruin",
      "Foreign workers' homes, schools, kitchens, and checkpoints became more inventive than the inner city while remaining classified as less civilized.",
      "A mural combines northern roof braces, desert shade cloth, and demonic repeating arches. The checkpoint report calls it visual disorder.",
      "Interior Passage Card",
      "Valid for useful outsiders between work bell and curfew. Innovation proposals must be reassigned to a citizen sponsor before consideration.",
      "Proud Traditionalist — official contempt contradicted by the maker's obvious dependence",
      worldChoice("Open the interior checkpoint", "strength", "The district's road stops dividing usefulness from belonging."),
      worldChoice("Catalog every borrowed design", "resistance", "Central self-sufficiency becomes impossible to claim honestly."),
      "Barbarus Mosaic Tile"),
    worldSite("AG", "Peregrinus", "central", 34, 24, "ruin",
      "Hostels, map rooms, messenger courts, and trade shrines prove all three human cultures remained interdependent.",
      "Travelers pinned recipes beside route changes. Half the atlas is roads; the rest is advice about soup.",
      "Mera's Source Page",
      "Four surviving-route annotations match Mera Quill's hand except for one older correction: DEMON ROAD, NOT EMPTY ROAD.",
      "Curious Seeker — layered travelers' voices, uncertainty retained rather than cleaned",
      worldChoice("Add your verified routes", "agility", "The atlas becomes current through admitted partial knowledge."),
      worldChoice("Carry a copy to every settlement", "defense", "No single archive keeps the only map."),
      "Peregrinus Route Leaf"),
    worldSite("AH", "Foederati", "central", 34, 28, "town",
      "A living settlement in allied barracks must write its first civic principle without pretending any rule is consequence-free.",
      "The council meets around a mess table because nobody can agree which ruined office deserves authority.",
      "Four Proposed First Rules",
      "Equal ration, contextual need, earned share, and rotating judgment each protect someone and burden someone else. Empty space waits beneath them for revision.",
      "Patient Mediator — dissent named beside beneficiaries and costs",
      worldChoice("Choose contextual need with public review", "defense", "Care becomes a rule that must explain itself."),
      worldChoice("Choose rotating judgment with appeal", "agility", "Authority moves before it can mistake itself for nature."),
      "Foederati First Charter"),
    worldSite("AI", "Hostis", "central", 34, 31, "ruin",
      "Prisons and interrogation courts collapsed demons, deserters, dissenters, and inconvenient witnesses into one category: enemy.",
      "A guard home shares a wall with Cell Twelve. Lullabies scratched through the plaster belong to both sides.",
      "Prisoner 8-Delta Testimony",
      "The Unbroken's projected behavior contained voluntary losses incompatible with optimal personal continuity. Classification: demon, anomalous. Confidence: sixty-eight percent.",
      "Exacting Keeper — demonic precision preserved by a human jailer who did not understand its implication",
      worldChoice("Separate every prisoner category", "resistance", "The archive regains distinctions that policy erased."),
      worldChoice("Open the evidence rooms first", "agility", "Claims are tested before inherited labels are repeated."),
      "Hostis Cell Counter"),
    worldSite("AJ", "Monstrum", "central", 31, 31, "ruin",
      "Quarantine homes, laboratories, creature yards, and a breach zone once distinguished illness, adaptation, and demonification before command named all three monster.",
      "An altered animal still sleeps beneath the blanket its handler repaired fourteen times.",
      "Classification Draft Seven",
      "Change is not evidence of hostile rule. Pain is not allegiance. This distinction was removed before military publication.",
      "Curious Seeker — careful hypotheses, tenderness disciplined into observation",
      worldChoice("Release the altered animal", "defense", "Uncertainty becomes freedom and a risk you accept."),
      worldChoice("End its unrelievable pain", "resistance", "Mercy takes a form with no comforting proof."),
      "Monstrum Handler's Needle"),
    worldSite("AK", "Prodigium", "central", 28, 31, "ruin",
      "Miracle vaults, failed instruments, and Moonmaiden reports connect true eclipses across regions while exposing institutional fraud.",
      "A fake moon relic is labeled AUTHENTIC in seven scripts. Somebody added NOT EVEN GOOD GLASS in an eighth.",
      "Moon-Favor Index",
      "The Hero's younger brother appears in favor records but not in the confirmed Moonmaiden rolls. The two lists were kept separately.",
      "Exacting Keeper — cross-dated evidence, unwilling to turn uncertainty into devotion",
      worldChoice("Expose the fraudulent claims", "resistance", "Grace becomes harder to own and easier to recognize honestly."),
      worldChoice("Repair the eclipse chronometer", "agility", "Separate legends begin sharing one measurable sky."),
      "Prodigium Eclipse Gear"),
    worldSite("AL", "Defensor", "central", 25, 31, "ruin",
      "Training yards, homes, mess halls, and memorials reconstruct the Ninth Bell through a hero, workers, rival, prisoner, dog, and evacuees.",
      "The legendary shield was a bakery door reinforced with two training spears. The bakery charged for it afterward.",
      "Six Accounts of the Ninth Bell",
      "No witness saw the whole stand. Together they show a frightened defender, a retreating rival, support crews, and civilians making the legendary minute possible.",
      "Protective Anchor — many concrete voices refusing a single clean hero",
      worldChoice("Restore all six accounts", "defense", "The legend grows more human without becoming smaller."),
      worldChoice("Rebuild the ordinary training yard", "strength", "Future defenders begin with practice instead of myth."),
      "Ninth Bell Door Hinge"),
    worldSite("AM", "Vindex", "central", 22, 31, "ruin",
      "A retaliation court converted every grief into an attack order.",
      "Petitioners brought food for long waits. The gallery has more surviving lunch tins than weapons.",
      "Unanswered Vengeance Petition",
      "My daughter is dead. I request a target large enough to resemble my loss. The clerk approved a village whose name I never learned.",
      "Fierce Idealist — grief preserved beside the machinery that exploited it",
      worldChoice("Carry the petition to descendants", "resistance", "The living inherit truth without an obligation to fulfill its violence."),
      worldChoice("Archive it as unanswered", "defense", "Pain is recognized without being converted into another command."),
      "Vindex Petition Weight"),
    worldSite("AN", "Devotio", "central", 23, 22, "ruin",
      "The oath plaza holds the burned mortal circle where the Sun descended, judged, and eventually died.",
      "Weeds grow through the exact center of the judgment mark. Nobody authorized them.",
      "The Hero's Doubt",
      "The Sun's verdict bound herself and the Demon King bodily while opening civilian corridors. He forced the wounded world to accept that the verdict bound him and that he had already survived it, stepped outside, and killed her while she held the exits open. The Hero later returned because Sun-favor gave certainty of action, never certainty that action made him good.",
      "Devotional Interpreter — worship that refuses to relieve its hero of responsibility",
      worldChoice("Restore the circle as a court", "defense", "Duty remains public and answerable."),
      worldChoice("Restore it as a garden", "agility", "The law's scar becomes a place that must be tended, changed, and shared."),
      "Devotio Mortal Ash"),

    worldSite("N", "The Forge's Path", "holy", 51, 19, "ruin",
      "Pilgrimage workshops repeat acts of making without purpose. Marriage tokens, apprentice marks, and broken road shrines lead toward evidence of the Forge's murder.",
      "One demonified hammer taps a cold nail forever. Beside it waits a chair whose fourth leg was measured but never cut.",
      "A Stranger's Unfinished Stool",
      "The maker wrote only: promised by sundown. Completing the leg restores no god and saves no army. It keeps one ordinary promise from remaining broken.",
      "Restless Builder — measurements, deadline, no surviving explanation of who needed the chair",
      worldChoice("Finish the stool by hand", "strength", "Purpose interrupts repetition; the workshop becomes still."),
      worldChoice("Teach another pilgrim the repair", "defense", "Making returns as a relationship rather than an inherited motion."),
      "Forge Road Hammer-Pin"),
    worldSite("Q", "The Sun's Descent", "holy", 36, 13, "ruin",
      "A straight ceremonial road loops because demonification preserved direction without judgment. Court fragments show the First Disciple resisted before the Sun descended.",
      "Pilgrims carried pocket rules for disputes. One says: if both people are furious, boil water before deciding who is right.",
      "First Disciple's Refusal",
      "She rejected the Demon King's necessity before any goddess appeared. The Sun found a mortal practice already alive; descent named it, but did not invent it.",
      "Fierce Idealist — furious eyewitness language, facts limited to the witnessed murder and argument",
      worldChoice("Follow the road's rule until it fails", "resistance", "You honor law long enough to understand its purpose."),
      worldChoice("Break the loop to protect the next traveler", "agility", "Circumstance corrects inherited direction."),
      "Sunroad Pocket Rule"),
    worldSite("BQ", "The Moon's Landing", "holy", 47, 5, "ruin",
      "Fallen roofs still hover inches above empty floors: remnants of the Moon's final power distributed through thousands of trivial rescues.",
      "A teacup sits unbroken beneath a beam suspended inches above the floor. A hand still reaches toward it from the dust.",
      "Ledger of Small Survivals",
      "Coordinated Demanders created more simultaneous disasters than one god could hold. One doorway stayed open. One fever broke. At Moon's Landing, the Demon King killed what remained of her while she held a final roof above people whose names were lost.",
      "Devotional Interpreter — collective testimony, no grand eyewitness and no claim that survival was fair",
      worldChoice("Lower the last roof safely", "strength", "The final remnant of her rescue becomes mortal work."),
      worldChoice("Preserve the tiny survivals by name", "defense", "Her death is remembered through people, not spectacle."),
      "Moonless Roof Shard"),

    worldSite("BH", "Journey's End", "desert", 40, 33, "ruin",
      "Pilgrim tokens, caravan memorials, the broken great road, and the Forge's last bridge ask whether an honest ending can count without perfection.",
      "Veyra's master's assessment stops halfway through the word adequate. The tool beside it is finished enough to work.",
      "The Forge's Bridge Pin",
      "The Forge used his hammer as the final bridge pin and refused to release the crossing. With both hands occupied, the Demon King killed him using a blade designed at Smoldering and made certain by a Demander. The last caravan crossed over his dying body.",
      "Proud Traditionalist — pilgrimage record, craft standards softened by witnessed sacrifice",
      worldChoice("Mark the unfinished tool complete", "resistance", "Completion becomes an honest judgment rather than unreachable purity."),
      worldChoice("Use the tool to repair the road", "strength", "Its worth is established through what it permits next."),
      "Forge's Final Bridge Pin"),
    worldSite("BI", "The Road Home", "desert", 43, 36, "ruin",
      "Return marks line a shifting caravan road. Travelers wrote what changed them before reentering family life.",
      "Some marks are profound. One says only: I learned not to buy dates from Kes.",
      "Blank Return Marker",
      "The stone waits for a sentence about the person returning, not a tally of miles conquered.",
      "Curious Seeker — layered travelers, each authoritative only about their own change",
      worldChoice("Write about your brother", "resistance", "You admit the dead still shape the road home."),
      worldChoice("Write about someone living", "defense", "Return becomes an obligation to a future, not only a grave."),
      "Road Home Marker"),
    worldSite("BJ", "Traveler's Hope", "desert", 46, 39, "ruin",
      "Shade engines, cisterns, repair stalls, guest courts, and a dried garden await a pump repair that can use knowledge from several cultures.",
      "The guest court enforces one rule: whoever complains about the shade must take the next repair shift.",
      "Three Pump Solutions",
      "Central tolerances, Northern bracing, and demonic pressure certainty can each move water. The original engineer left room for whichever knowledge arrived.",
      "Restless Builder — delighted technical pluralism, no loyalty to a single school's pride",
      worldChoice("Build with the parts you gathered", "strength", "Water returns through connected knowledge."),
      worldChoice("Leave all three methods in the manual", "agility", "The next repairer inherits alternatives, not doctrine."),
      "Traveler's Hope Pump Seal"),
    worldSite("BK", "The First Step", "desert", 49, 42, "ruin",
      "Apprentice houses and a ceremonial road serve young people preparing to leave despite the dying world.",
      "A mile marker holds three bundles of spoiled food. Each is tied with a different family's knot.",
      "One-Mile Request",
      "Escort Nemi to the first marker. No monster is expected. Reward: one repaired strap and her mother's gratitude, whether or not either feels legendary.",
      "Practical Caretaker — request-board plainness, danger neither invented nor dismissed",
      worldChoice("Walk the single mile beside Nemi", "defense", "A small request receives full attention."),
      worldChoice("Teach her how to read the first storm", "agility", "The escort ends with more independence than it began."),
      "First-Step Sand Strap"),
    worldSite("BL", "The Good Traveler", "desert", 40, 20, "ruin",
      "A trade stop followed the rule 'leave the road better,' with both sincere maintenance and enthusiastic market scams.",
      "A cup is labeled ANCIENT IMPERIAL RELIC. Fresh clay beneath the paint suggests it became ancient yesterday.",
      "Seven Percent Genuine",
      "Kes certifies that the cup contains authentic dust from somewhere old. The percentage is technically nonzero. The repaired road beside his stall is entirely genuine.",
      "Opportunistic Broker — shameless sales logic, real communal labor kept off the invoice",
      worldChoice("Repair the next travel marker", "strength", "You leave the road better without needing the claim to be pure."),
      worldChoice("Expose the cup and keep the joke", "resistance", "Truth does not require erasing the person who exaggerated it."),
      "Seven-Percent Cup"),
    worldSite("BM", "Adventure's Beginning", "desert", 45, 23, "ruin",
      "Guide houses, request boards, outfitters, taverns, and flattering monster trophies turn departure into both livelihood and story.",
      "A terrifying horned beast plaque covers the remains of a very ordinary goat stall.",
      "Three Spools of Blue",
      "An adventurer solved a missing-dye request by mending a loom, bargaining with a rival, and noticing which child kept blue thread around one wrist. No sword appears in the account.",
      "Curious Seeker — request notes that value attention over scale",
      worldChoice("Complete the abandoned small request", "agility", "Observation succeeds where combat would have had nothing to strike."),
      worldChoice("Restore the honest request board", "defense", "Need no longer has to sound heroic to deserve help."),
      "Blue Thread Spool"),
    worldSite("BN", "Journeyman's Rest", "desert", 46, 27, "town",
      "Veyra's living settlement of workshops, markets, courts, caravans, and unfinished projects can become the world's outward-moving recovery hub.",
      "Every workshop door bears two marks: the master's old standard and the apprentice's first alteration.",
      "Veyra's Own Mark",
      "She waited years for a dead master's permission to call her work finished. Today she stamps the tool herself, then gives the bench to a student.",
      "Restless Builder — impatient craft language, grief redirected into teaching",
      worldChoice("Witness Veyra claim completion", "resistance", "A living person stops asking the dead to certify her future."),
      worldChoice("Help prepare the apprentice bench", "strength", "The workshop's next life begins in material work."),
      "Veyra's First Master Mark"),
    worldSite("BO", "Destination's Beginning", "desert", 47, 31, "ruin",
      "A retirement district treated completed journeys as beginnings for family, research, teaching, and entirely different work.",
      "A former dragon hunter became famous locally for growing pears shaped like disappointed faces.",
      "Second-Vocation Register",
      "Stopped adventuring is not listed as a failure condition. Entries continue with teacher, parent, bad poet, bridge inspector, and finally slept well.",
      "Enduring Realist — dry civic register, respect expressed through unadorned continuation",
      worldChoice("Add retirement to the route book", "resistance", "Survival becomes a destination worthy of a map."),
      worldChoice("Restore the teaching courtyard", "defense", "Experience remains useful after danger stops defining it."),
      "Second-Vocation Badge"),
    worldSite("BP", "Pathfinder", "desert", 40, 27, "ruin",
      "A guide academy, rescue posts, map labyrinth, and occupied tower honor a pathfinder whose greatest decision was turning back.",
      "The heroic statue points forward. Wind has rotated its metal finger until it now indicates the safe route home.",
      "Original Expedition Report",
      "Visibility failed. Objective probability fell below the cost of eleven lives. I ordered retreat. Everyone returned. Later copies changed retreat to strategic circuit.",
      "Guarded Watcher — weather, probability, and responsibility without apology",
      worldChoice("Publish the original report", "resistance", "Turning back enters history as courage rather than embarrassment."),
      worldChoice("Rotate the statue toward home", "strength", "The monument finally points where its subject chose to go."),
      "Pathfinder's Return Compass"),

    worldSite("AO", "Libertas", "demon", 6, 24, "ruin",
      "A failed Central colony of survey offices, settler homes, and mission courts called inhabited demonic land empty.",
      "A child's garden fills the foundation of a displaced household. Two sets of names are scratched into the same threshold.",
      "Vacancy Certification",
      "No human residents observed. Indigenous demonic households are classified as nonresidential continuity functions and therefore do not affect vacancy.",
      "Exacting Keeper — colonial precision exposing the definition that made removal legal",
      worldChoice("Mark every displaced household", "resistance", "Human wrongdoing remains visible beside ancient demon crimes."),
      worldChoice("Preserve the settler children's names too", "defense", "Accountability does not require declaring ordinary lives unreal."),
      "Libertas Survey Chain"),
    worldSite("AP", "The Knife", "demon", 6, 28, "ruin",
      "A demonic counter-settlement cut Libertas's logistics and recorded combatants, civilians, and uncertain deaths without remorse.",
      "Meal portions were recalculated after every killing because fewer enemy mouths changed siege projections.",
      "Kill Register K-19",
      "Confirmed combatants: 42. Confirmed civilians: 17. Uncertain: 9. Precision does not express regret, but it prevents the crime from disappearing into a heroic total.",
      "Exacting Keeper — demonic count, emotionally neutral, evidentially complete within stated confidence",
      worldChoice("Preserve the exact categories", "resistance", "Numbers expose what their author did not morally condemn."),
      worldChoice("Add the victims' recovered names", "defense", "Human remembrance joins demonic measure without replacing it."),
      "Knife Register Stylus"),
    worldSite("AQ", "Progredior", "demon", 4, 23, "ruin",
      "Forward forts, family plots, schools, and an unfinished triumph arch became sincere homes inside an invasion.",
      "A school primer asks children to draw the empty land. One child drew the demonic neighbor who traded for salt.",
      "Settler's Kitchen Wall",
      "We knew the claim was contested. We also knew the stove smoked less than the one at home. Both facts remained true while we hung the curtains.",
      "Practical Caretaker — domestic record with no authority over the colony's justice",
      worldChoice("Preserve the homes and name the invasion", "resistance", "Ordinary life remains real without sanitizing its foundation."),
      worldChoice("Give the school records to Correctors", "agility", "The next generation inherits contradiction instead of triumph."),
      "Progredior Curtain Ring"),
    worldSite("AR", "The Cloak", "demon", 2, 27, "ruin",
      "Hidden tunnels, caches, observation cells, and human contraband show demons learning decoys and irregular tactics.",
      "Copied jokes deteriorate in each tactical manual until the final version classifies laughter as an evasive signal.",
      "Adaptive Tactics Revision",
      "Human deception increased survival by fourteen percent. Replication succeeded for three generations, then variation declined after human sources vanished.",
      "Restless Builder — demonic worldation narrowing into inherited repetition",
      worldChoice("Restore the human source notes", "agility", "Copied invention regains context and alternatives."),
      worldChoice("Open the tunnels as a shared route", "strength", "A hiding system becomes connection rather than ambush."),
      "Cloak Decoy Thread"),
    worldSite("AS", "The Night", "demon", 3, 32, "town",
      "An active demon settlement maintains heat, food, patrol, and records without performing hospitality for human comfort.",
      "Demon children play probability games by predicting which heated tile an adult will choose. They cheer only by updating the odds loudly.",
      "Terms of Temporary Entry",
      "No affection is offered. No hostility is assumed. Trade remains valid while both parties meet stated obligations.",
      "Patient Mediator — exact bargain, cultural translation without false warmth",
      worldChoice("Trade under the exact terms", "resistance", "Peace begins as reliable behavior, not emotional resemblance."),
      worldChoice("Offer a revisable route compact", "agility", "Continuity accepts a mechanism for correction."),
      "Night Settlement Heat Token"),
    worldSite("AT", "The Scare", "demon", 5, 36, "ruin",
      "A former human warning post became bait. Teren-Seven identifies which fires are traps, then offers a bargain with no appeal to friendship.",
      "A low blue fire burns behind a stone screen facing away from the road. The abandoned decoy braziers are three times its size.",
      "Teren-Seven's Bargain",
      "If you leave the east cache untouched, I will guide you through three active kill routes. Compliance remains optimal even after you learn the cache could feed you.",
      "Exacting Keeper — demonic terms, motives fully stated and trust tested through action",
      worldChoice("Honor the bargain when breaking it is easier", "resistance", "Trust forms from chosen reliability across difference."),
      worldChoice("Renegotiate before touching the cache", "agility", "Need changes the terms without pretending no promise existed."),
      "Teren-Seven's Route Model"),
    worldSite("AU", "The Fallen", "demon", 9, 37, "ruin",
      "A grave-flat repurposed remains by function until the Unbroken secretly restored names from both species.",
      "One human marker and one demon marker share the same carefully replaced stone base.",
      "The Unbroken's Name List",
      "Names provide no measurable advantage to the dead. He restored them anyway, then returned years later when wind erased three.",
      "Protective Anchor — cross-species names, maker unidentified, motive inferable but not explained",
      worldChoice("Restore the remaining names", "strength", "A useless act becomes a chosen continuity."),
      worldChoice("Add the unknown without guessing", "resistance", "Absence is recorded as absence rather than filled with a comforting lie."),
      "Two-Species Grave Chisel"),
    worldSite("AV", "The Hunt", "demon", 1, 9, "ruin",
      "A rally site in demon territory close to the Northern border reconstructs the Academy assault through barracks, route tables, pens, and calculations.",
      "The survey begins at the western edge, counts one coordinate inward and nine south, then draws a straight measured line toward the Academy road.",
      "Academy Suppression Model",
      "Territorial gain ranked third. Primary objective: reduce the human institution's rate of producing unpredictable high-impact leaders.",
      "Exacting Keeper — operational logic, no access to the human experience of the attack",
      worldChoice("Carry the model to the Academy", "resistance", "The ruin gains its attacker's reason without surrendering its own truth."),
      worldChoice("Destroy the remaining beast pens", "strength", "The old assault mechanism cannot be repeated here."),
      "Hunt Route Table"),
    worldSite("BB", "The Reach", "demon", 3, 48, "ruin",
      "A Crown Remainder stronghold repeats inherited architecture and expects the strongest fighter to become the next stable ruler.",
      "Every new arch is copied from an older one. Small errors accumulate because nobody is authorized to propose a different arch.",
      "Corrector Leadership Model",
      "A system that selected strength and reached near-extinction contains a demonstrated fault. Continuity requires revisable selection, not a stronger repetition.",
      "Fierce Idealist — demonic logic sharpened into systemic dissent",
      worldChoice("Support revisable leadership", "defense", "Demons pursue continuity by allowing correction."),
      worldChoice("Defeat the claimant and refuse the crown", "strength", "Strength proves it can decline the role their system predicts."),
      "Reach Correction Counter"),
    worldSite("BC", "The Rest", "demon", 18, 48, "ruin",
      "A grave-flat continuity laboratory moves bodies by inherited command without restoring personhood.",
      "One body still sweeps around the outline where its home used to stand.",
      "Function Without Person",
      "Motion persisted. Memory, preference, and self-correction did not. Classify outcome as maintained infrastructure, not resurrection.",
      "Enduring Realist — demonic lab note precise enough to reject its own desired conclusion",
      worldChoice("Shut the command down", "resistance", "Rest is allowed to mean an ending."),
      worldChoice("Preserve only the evidence mechanism", "agility", "The warning survives without continuing the bodies' use."),
      "Rest Command Spindle"),
    worldSite("BD", "Charred Ruins", "demon", 28, 43, "ruin",
      "Works and Protection once joined industrial invention with civic defense. Repair constructs now obey contradictory orders.",
      "An imperial kettle automatically reinforces its handle every hour. It has become mostly handle.",
      "Human Design, Demon Iteration",
      "Human proposals generated novel forms. Demonic calibration made them reproducible. Neither half alone produced the empire remembered afterward.",
      "Restless Builder — collaborative workshop record, credit retained across species",
      worldChoice("Resolve the constructs' competing orders", "agility", "Purpose returns where repetition had consumed it."),
      worldChoice("Recover the god-killing tool pattern", "resistance", "You preserve dangerous evidence without confusing knowledge for innocence."),
      "Charred Calibration Tool"),
    worldSite("BE", "Smoldering Ruins", "demon", 36, 44, "ruin",
      "Possibility and Exchange held markets, proposals, performances, prototypes, and transit. It most clearly shows what stagnated after humans left.",
      "A prototype umbrella opens downward. Three sales pitches insist this is intentional.",
      "Proposal Court Rejections",
      "Most ideas failed. Enough succeeded to change four cities. After the exodus, proposals declined while replication accuracy remained high.",
      "Opportunistic Broker — lively pitches and skeptical calculations sharing one archive",
      worldChoice("Reopen the proposal floor", "agility", "Failure becomes permissible again."),
      worldChoice("Carry unfinished designs to Veyra", "strength", "Old possibility meets living craft without being copied blindly."),
      "Smoldering Prototype Hinge"),
    worldSite("BF", "Sizzling Ruins", "demon", 38, 46, "ruin",
      "Memory and Measure contains calibration courts, the Record Keeper's office, and the only council archive that proves the witness purge. Its High Council was entirely demonic: harmony was real, but political authority was never equal.",
      "Every corrected number remains visible beneath the next. The deepest sheet is sewn into the binding with black wire.",
      "Council Authorization: Corrected Copy",
      "The council authorized elimination of witnesses and an engineered disaster across all four hearts. The future Demon King recorded the order; he did not need to invent it later.",
      "Exacting Keeper — primary council record, complete on authorization but silent about every victim's experience",
      worldChoice("Preserve the guilty version", "resistance", "Continuity is forced to carry the proof of its own crime."),
      worldChoice("Copy it into human archives", "agility", "No species keeps exclusive custody of the truth."),
      "Sizzling Correction Plate"),
    worldSite("BG", "Boiling Ruins", "demon", 39, 44, "ruin",
      "Life and Provision held gardens, clinics, kitchens, seed banks, waterworks, and reservoirs: one of four equal hearts, not a lesser tragedy.",
      "A geothermal nursery schedule includes an argument over whether children should be permitted to name every bean.",
      "Raw Provision Ledger",
      "Supplies were sufficient during evacuation. The Record Keeper's scarcity claim was fabricated to justify a killing whose real purpose was stolen emotion.",
      "Practical Caretaker — primary quantities, ordinary allocation notes, decisive within its narrow domain",
      worldChoice("Preserve the unadjusted ledgers", "resistance", "The oldest manufactured necessity loses its cover."),
      worldChoice("Recover seed for living settlements", "defense", "Truth and provision leave the ruin together."),
      "Boiling Seed Measure"),

    worldSite("S", "Central Command", "outer", 18, 28, "ruin",
      "War rooms, kitchens, maps, hospitals, desertion court, and evacuation routes show a command that never promised killing the Demon King would heal the world.",
      "The Hero's table wobbled. Three folded casualty estimates kept it level through the final briefing.",
      "Final Objective Order",
      "The gods will remain dead. The land will remain wounded. Kill the Demon King because delay increases the lives he can still take—not because one death repairs all others.",
      "Protective Anchor — the Hero's direct order, certain about the objective and explicit about its limits",
      worldChoice("Publish the order without victory rhetoric", "resistance", "Necessity remains narrow and accountable."),
      worldChoice("Reopen the evacuation route", "defense", "Command serves survival after command itself is gone."),
      "Hero's Map-Table Wedge"),
    worldSite("T", "Daemonium Hills", "outer", 18, 31, "ruin",
      "Trenches, medic gullies, stakes, banners, and demon counterworks reconstruct ordinary units creating the openings attributed to one Hero.",
      "A cook's ladle was sharpened into a digging tool and then bent back into a ladle.",
      "Opening Fourteen",
      "The Hero crossed at 18:40. Before that minute, two ditch crews, a false banner team, and unnamed medics moved the battlefield into the shape he needed.",
      "Exacting Keeper — synchronized unit logs, no single narrator with the whole view",
      worldChoice("Restore the support-unit markers", "strength", "The battlefield shows how many hands made one opening."),
      worldChoice("Add the unnamed as unknown", "resistance", "Missing names are not replaced with invented certainty."),
      "Daemonium Ditch Spoon"),
    worldSite("U", "Fort Unum", "outer", 14, 31, "ruin",
      "One fort held an approach until its defenders were spent while a support unit withdrew with the wounded. Both choices were required.",
      "The memorial tower key and supply-escape key are the same key. History separated what the builders joined.",
      "Two Necessary Orders",
      "Hold the east stair. Withdraw the west infirmary. No later account may call either unit coward or sacrifice without naming the other.",
      "Protective Anchor — command language designed to prevent one duty consuming another",
      worldChoice("Open the supply route first", "defense", "The fort is entered through the lives carried out."),
      worldChoice("Open the memorial first, then the route", "resistance", "You accept the power and danger of symbolic order."),
      "Fort Unum Double Key"),
    worldSite("V", "Fort Duae", "outer", 14, 28, "ruin",
      "The second fort was deliberately surrendered so its collapse would narrow pursuit and buy the spear time.",
      "Retreat arrows remain beneath later paint that labels the same corridors LAST STAND.",
      "Surrender Geometry",
      "The commander selected the loss of a fort over the loss of its people. Public history changed this to defeat because planned retreat was judged harmful to morale.",
      "Guarded Watcher — tactical report, emotion absent but choices clear",
      worldChoice("Reveal the retreat route", "agility", "Withdrawal returns to the vocabulary of courage."),
      worldChoice("Reinforce the surviving escape tunnel", "strength", "The fort's truest purpose becomes usable again."),
      "Fort Duae Retreat Arrow"),
    worldSite("BA", "Plains of Bellum", "outer", 18, 34, "ruin",
      "An army spread into useful directions. Graves, packs, markers, and Sare's living construction of her own legend show symbols and bodies supporting each other.",
      "One famous banner pole is a laundry line. Nobody corrected the painting because the banner mattered by then.",
      "Mass Marker Without Names",
      "Unit totals reconcile; personal names do not. A later hand added: a formation is made of people even when the archive loses the order they stood in.",
      "Proud Traditionalist — military memorial language corrected by a survivor's hand",
      worldChoice("Restore the recoverable names", "defense", "A useful symbol makes room for the bodies beneath it."),
      worldChoice("Leave space for names still unknown", "resistance", "The marker admits the archive is incomplete."),
      "Bellum Laundry Banner"),
    worldSite("W", "Hellhold", "inner", 11, 31, "ruin",
      "Prison cells, fuel vaults, body stores, breach tunnels, and a small survivors' route show an army opening a prison it could not fully empty.",
      "A trapped demonic prisoner mapped a human escape because six survivors increased the probability that someone would later open its own cell.",
      "Mutual Exit Calculation",
      "Assistance is not friendship. Your survival creates a fourteen percent future release chance. Mine creates a guide through the fuel tunnel. Agreement remains favorable.",
      "Opportunistic Broker — exact self-interest producing real aid without sentimental translation",
      worldChoice("Free the prisoner under exact terms", "agility", "Cooperation remains meaningful without pretending affection."),
      worldChoice("Open the survivors' route first", "defense", "Immediate vulnerable lives take precedence without denying the bargain."),
      "Hellhold Shared Latch"),
    worldSite("AW", "The Screams", "inner", 16, 37, "ruin",
      "Acoustic tunnels, abandoned medical posts, and separated squads repeat voices that may be wind, ghost, or demonification.",
      "If adopted, the cat ignores three cries and hisses at the fourth. The fourth is attached to something still alive.",
      "Medic's Echo Test",
      "Repeated sound does not change when answered. Living pain does. We cannot save every voice, but we can stop treating all of them as identical.",
      "Practical Caretaker — field test born from unbearable triage",
      worldChoice("Follow the changing voice", "defense", "Attention finds the one danger still capable of an answer."),
      worldChoice("Mark the repeating tunnels", "agility", "Future travelers inherit a distinction instead of your fear."),
      "Screams Resonance Fork"),
    worldSite("AX", "The Madness", "inner", 19, 37, "ruin",
      "Contradictory Demands and stolen emotional residue made soldiers turn on one another without erasing the choices made inside that pressure.",
      "Two bodies wear different uniforms. A single rope joins their belts with a knot pulled tight from both sides.",
      "Pressure and Choice Report",
      "External compulsion increased rage and certainty. It did not produce identical actions. Magical pressure is causal. It is not a complete moral verdict.",
      "Enduring Realist — clinical survivor testimony resisting both total blame and total absolution",
      worldChoice("Carry both causes together", "resistance", "You refuse a simple innocence that would also erase choice."),
      worldChoice("Cut the repeating Demand anchors", "strength", "The site loses part of its power to force one answer."),
      "Madness Binding Knot"),
    worldSite("AY", "The Gates", "inner", 18, 40, "ruin",
      "The final barrier holds the Hero's whetstone, unsent note, and last ordered retreat. No honorable collective death was requested here.",
      "If adopted, the cat stops. It will not enter the Fear. Waiting can also be loyalty.",
      "Unsent Note to My Brother",
      "If I do not return, do not make my ending into your occupation. I wanted you beside me. I never wanted you buried in the same minute.",
      "Protective Anchor — the Hero privately contradicting the legend built from his public certainty",
      worldChoice("Accept the cat's refusal to follow", "defense", "Love does not require identical destinations."),
      worldChoice("Sharpen the Old Sword without an oath", "resistance", "You prepare to enter without promising to remain forever."),
      "Hero's Last Whetstone"),
    worldSite("AZ", "The Fear", "final", 18, 43, "ruin",
      "The Demon King's death scar contains the Hero's ghost, unstable stolen emotions, and the place where victory became an endless role.",
      "Nothing here is a throne room. It is a wound shaped like the last thing two brothers knew how to do together.",
      "Memory-Clash",
      "Care, Duty, Limitation, Trust, Truth, and Future do not defeat grief. Together they let grief stop pretending that repetition is devotion.",
      "Protective Anchor — a surviving brother's account, limited to what he saw and chose",
      worldChoice("Meet your brother as a person", "resistance", "The final battle becomes a conversation with an ending."),
      worldChoice("Lay down the role before the sword", "defense", "Love remains after occupation and obligation release their claim."),
      "Moonless Sword Bloom")
  ];

  var worldSitesByCode = {};
  worldSiteList.forEach(function (site) {
    worldSitesByCode[site.code] = site;
  });

  var worldSiteEnemyOverrides = {
    A: "starvingWolf", B: "goblinScout", C: "wraith", D: "starvingWolf", E: "goblinFighter",
    F: "demonHound", G: "goblinFighter", H: "goblinScout", I: "banditRaider", J: "frostBear",
    K: "starvingWolf", L: "wanderingDemon", M: "academyEcho", O: "banditRaider", P: "frostStag"
  };
  Object.keys(worldSiteEnemyOverrides).forEach(function (code) {
    worldSitesByCode[code].enemy = worldSiteEnemyOverrides[code];
  });

  var worldAcademyNodes = [
    { id: "gate", name: "Broken Gate", route: "center", text: "Cart ruts pass beneath the broken arch. Initials have been cut into the stone from a child's knee height to well above your head.", next: ["founder", "service"] },
    { id: "founder", name: "Founder's Walk", route: "west", text: "A relief shows a child holding his sister's wrist. His other hand grips a weapon longer than he is tall. A round silver disk hangs above them.", next: ["classroom", "hall"] },
    { id: "classroom", name: "First Classroom", route: "west", text: "Desks form a circle. One surviving line on the wall reads: POWER IS WHAT ARRIVES. COURAGE IS WHAT YOU CHOOSE BEFORE AND AFTER IT LEAVES.", evidence: "roll1", next: ["kitchen", "yard"] },
    { id: "kitchen", name: "Communal Kitchen", route: "west", text: "Training schedules share the wall with complaints about porridge. A scratched note awards someone named Pell the right to add salt.", item: "Academy Salt Cup", next: ["archive"] },
    { id: "hall", name: "Hall of Unfinished Heroes", route: "west", text: "Labels beneath the portraits read EXPELLED, RETIRED, AFRAID, CHANGED VOCATION, and STILL TRYING.", evidence: "roll2", next: ["archive"] },
    { id: "service", name: "Service Court", route: "east", text: "Laundry hooks line one wall. A cistern, delivery marks, and repair benches fill the yard below them.", next: ["infirmary", "dormitory"] },
    { id: "infirmary", name: "Evacuation Infirmary", route: "east", text: "Every bed faces the eastern exit. Carrying straps remain buckled beneath the mattresses.", item: "Academy Field Wrap", next: ["stair"] },
    { id: "dormitory", name: "Lower Dormitory", route: "east", text: "Thirty-three hooks bear student names. Two larger hooks bear staff names. Several pegs remain unlettered.", evidence: "roll3", next: ["stair"] },
    { id: "stair", name: "Collapsed Evacuation Stair", route: "east", text: "Old repair dates cover the supports. The lowest beam split beneath a newer iron brace, and the whole stair fell toward the exit.", next: ["yard"] },
    { id: "yard", name: "Training Yard", route: "center", text: "A human shape crosses the yard and repeats the same measured strike. Its feet return to the same two patches of dust.", enemy: "academyDrillEcho", next: ["bell", "armory"] },
    { id: "bell", name: "Signal Bell", route: "center", text: "The rope ends in a nest of torn fibers. They lean toward the building, away from the bell.", item: "Academy Bell Fiber", next: ["armory"] },
    { id: "armory", name: "Open Armory", route: "center", text: "The racks stand open. Empty brackets are marked with names and hurried fingerprints.", evidence: "roll4", next: ["breach"] },
    { id: "archive", name: "Founder's Archive", route: "west", text: "A founding charter bears the same child-and-silver-disk seal as the relief outside. The first line names the Northern Academy of Heroes.", next: ["maproom"] },
    { id: "maproom", name: "Rescue Map Room", route: "west", text: "Pins and faded thread lead toward the Forest of Screams. Three routes are marked ATTEMPTED. None is marked RETURNED.", next: ["breach"] },
    { id: "breach", name: "Demon Breach", route: "center", text: "The wall fell inward. Claw marks stop at circles of blackened stone, each circle the same width.", enemy: "academyBreachEcho", next: ["laststand"] },
    { id: "laststand", name: "Last Practice Hall", route: "center", text: "Chalk lines form a narrow lane to the east door. Nineteen tally marks have been cut into the doorframe.", next: ["rollcall"] },
    { id: "rollcall", name: "Roll Call Chamber", route: "center", text: "Four torn roll-call pages fit beneath a brass weight. Their edges match.", requiresEvidence: 4, next: ["overlook"] },
    { id: "overlook", name: "Northern Overlook", route: "center", text: "Stalwart's roofs are visible below. Smoke rises through patched boards. Footprints cross the Academy's old service road.", final: true, next: [] }
  ];

  var worldAcademyEvidence = {
    roll1: { title: "Roll Call I", text: "Nine students assigned west. Seven answered at second bell. Two listed moving civilians.", voice: "Exacting Keeper" },
    roll2: { title: "Roll Call II", text: "Eleven assigned center. Five answered. Three names appear later on infirmary tags; the remaining status is unknown.", voice: "Guarded Watcher" },
    roll3: { title: "Roll Call III", text: "Thirteen assigned east with two staff. All fifteen reached the dormitory. Six then returned toward the stair.", voice: "Protective Anchor" },
    roll4: { title: "Roll Call IV", text: "Final correction: thirty-three students. Two staff. Others still unknown.", voice: "Enduring Realist" }
  };

  var worldMinorGodFragments = {
    AG: { title: "Last Scribe's Extra Line", text: "The goddess divided herself across unfinished records. No whole consciousness answers, but a dying courier's sentence occasionally completes in a second hand.", voice: "Exacting Keeper", boundary: "Later archivists compare handwriting; they cannot establish divine consciousness." },
    K: { title: "Lantern Left Burning", text: "He spent his descended presence guiding refugees through the last blackouts. The last lantern went dark. Whether that was death or the completion of his promise remains disputed.", voice: "Devotional Interpreter", boundary: "The route record proves the lights; it does not prove what the final darkness meant." },
    H: { title: "Deepwell's Future Echo", text: "Deepwell never fully descended. Some wells return echoes that have not happened yet, but no surviving prayer receives a direct answer.", voice: "Guarded Watcher", boundary: "The listener recorded an impossible echo, not the god's present condition." },
    Z: { title: "Stitchmother's Hidden Repair", text: "Stitchmother surrendered divinity, lived one last generation as a mortal seamstress, and died after teaching every repair she knew. No grave admits which seamstress she was.", voice: "Practical Caretaker", boundary: "The craft lineage is documented; the anonymous mortal identity remains tradition." },
    AA: { title: "Third Voice's Unwanted Answer", text: "Third Voice dissolved his name into compromise. When enemies independently speak the same third solution, nobody can prove whether a god remains or people finally learned the habit.", voice: "Patient Mediator", boundary: "The record preserves matching proposals without assigning their cause." },
    BC: { title: "Gentle Dark's Missing Road", text: "Gentle Dark descended to guide the unprecedented dead. The Demon King killed her so his victims could not carry testimony beyond him. Without her road, some ghosts remain tied to unresolved bonds.", voice: "Devotional Interpreter", boundary: "Funerary failures support the missing road; no witness followed the dead far enough to map it." },
    BL: { title: "Crooked Coin's Refusal", text: "Crooked Coin never established one stable mortal anchor. Impossible luck may be his survival, his corpse twitching, or ordinary chance with excellent publicity.", voice: "Opportunistic Broker", boundary: "Every version benefits the person selling the coin." },
    P: { title: "The Peeping Laugh", text: "A knowing laugh follows a private reconciliation. It proves only that the old habit still manifests—not whether its shamelessly respectful god lives, died, or found a loophole.", voice: "Curious Seeker", boundary: "The witness heard a laugh. The god kept the quarrel's secret." }
  };
  Object.keys(worldMinorGodFragments).forEach(function (code) {
    worldSitesByCode[code].minorGod = worldMinorGodFragments[code];
  });

  var worldUnbrokenClues = {
    M: { title: "The Man Who Never Shivered", text: "Northern stories say he carried children through snow, divided food into exact portions, slept upright, and heard one missing traveler in the changed sound of a marching line.", voice: "Proud Traditionalist" },
    AG: { title: "The First Counter-Witness", text: "Central art remembers a human officer who argued in conditional proofs, never moral appeals. His face appears only in profile. Commentators call it early legal austerity.", voice: "Exacting Keeper" },
    BI: { title: "The Walker Without Thirst", text: "Desert stories claim he crossed open ground without drinking, selected camps by exact intervals, and tied identical sandal repairs across decades.", voice: "Guarded Watcher" },
    Q: { title: "The Guide Who Would Not Choose", text: "Holy histories praise his humility when he refused to name the correct god. Another reading is stranger: he would not let his logical endorsement become a system humans obeyed instead of choosing.", voice: "Devotional Interpreter" },
    AI: { title: "Continuity Actor U-0", text: "An ancient demonic identifier records a lifespan incompatible with human histories and classifies refugee care as a system-preservation deviation.", voice: "Exacting Keeper" }
  };
  Object.keys(worldUnbrokenClues).forEach(function (code) {
    worldSitesByCode[code].unbrokenClue = worldUnbrokenClues[code];
  });

  worldSitesByCode.AR.historyFragment = {
    title: "First Recorded Battle Boundary Survey",
    text: "The oldest reliable survey places the human-demon break inside Demon territory near the future Central and Desert borders. The Unbroken led the humans to victory; defeated demons then treated the Record Keeper's emerging power as the strongest available continuity model.",
    voice: "Exacting Keeper",
    boundary: "The later survey identifies the border relationship and allegiance shift, not the battlefield's exact coordinate or later name."
  };

  var worldShrines = [
    { id: "stalwart_child", name: "The Stalwart Child", regions: ["north"], text: "A little boy stands before his parents and sister with both arms spread. Above him, the Moon covers the Sun. A fallen general's helmet rests at his feet.", voice: "Protective Anchor", reward: { moonCharms: 1 } },
    { id: "thawmother", name: "The Thawmother", regions: ["north"], text: "Bel carried heated stones between twelve frozen seed cellars while labor began. For one night every footprint became warm soil. Later she was best known for charging neighbors replacement fees for borrowed tools.", voice: "Practical Caretaker", reward: { winterRoot: 2 } },
    { id: "bell_son", name: "The Bell Son", regions: ["north"], text: "A teenage watchman swung his body against a broken bell until moonlight carried the warning through an avalanche. With one deaf ear, he later designed visual signals so nobody would need his miracle again.", voice: "Restless Builder", reward: { scrapIronPieces: 2 } },
    { id: "first_moonmaiden", name: "The First Moonmaiden", regions: ["holy"], text: "Years after she rejected the Record Keeper's culling, the first disciple stood between refugee groups fighting over water. The eclipse stopped every weapon without killing its wielder. North calls it care, Central judgment, and Desert a fourth road.", voice: "Devotional Interpreter", reward: { moonCharms: 1 } },
    { id: "every_door", name: "The Prisoner Who Opened Every Door", regions: ["central"], text: "A deserter returned for the prison keys when demons entered Hostis. Moonlight opened every lock: dissidents, demons, killers, debtors, and hiding guards. The law pardoned her and then tried to prosecute whom she freed.", voice: "Fierce Idealist", reward: { medicine: 1 } },
    { id: "three_laws", name: "The Child Under Three Laws", regions: ["central"], text: "A child faced three true orders assigning one bridge to different groups. They changed the signals; the Moon made the bridge long enough. For sixty years the child designed forms with a box for CONFLICT WITH ANOTHER TRUE ORDER.", voice: "Patient Mediator", reward: { scrapIronPieces: 1, gold: 3 } },
    { id: "sand_father", name: "The Sand Father", regions: ["desert"], text: "A father searched a storm for the caravan carrying his estranged son. The Moon turned sand into a map. He saved twenty-four people. Reconciliation with his son still took nine years.", voice: "Enduring Realist", reward: { waterskin: 1 } },
    { id: "blue_thread", name: "The Blue-Thread Thief", regions: ["desert"], text: "A thief used stolen ceremonial thread to guide children from a burning market. The eclipse made each strand unbreakable. She returned the unused thread, served her sentence, and became an intolerable fire inspector.", voice: "Opportunistic Broker", reward: { medicine: 1, gold: 2 } },
    { id: "libertas_stranger", name: "The Stranger at Libertas", regions: ["demon"], text: "A human translator warned demonic families that Central soldiers planned to burn their tunnel. Moonlight carried her and the children through human lines. Demon records call her an unexplained human deviation; neither side kept her name.", voice: "Guarded Watcher", reward: { medicine: 1 } },
    { id: "last_standard", name: "The Last Standard-Bearer", regions: ["outer", "inner", "final"], text: "A wounded soldier walked backward toward scattered wounded so they could see the retreat banner. Battlefield dates cannot prove whether the Moon still lived; the figure may be Sare, another soldier, or a composite.", voice: "Protective Anchor", reward: { northernFieldWrap: 1 } }
  ];

var WORLD_VERSION = 1;
  var WORLD_MEMORIES = ["Care", "Duty", "Limitation", "Trust", "Truth", "Future"];
  var WORLD_TOWNS = ["A", "G", "O", "AH", "BN"];

  function freshWorldState() {
    return {
      version: WORLD_VERSION,
      routeBook: false,
      routeChoice: "",
      cat: { met: false, adopted: false, name: "the cat" },
      places: {},
      evidence: [],
      items: [],
      memories: { Care: false, Duty: false, Limitation: false, Trust: false, Truth: false, Future: false },
      regionVisits: {},
      connections: [],
      shrinesSeen: [],
      activeSite: "A",
      activeNode: "arrival",
      activeMode: "site",
      pendingEncounter: null,
      academy: { nodes: {}, evidence: [], active: "gate", resolved: false },
      commonGround: { revealed: false, visited: false },
      tulip: { found: false, carried: false, leftAtCommonGround: false, destination: "" },
      swordStage: 0,
      terenTrust: false,
      unbrokenSeen: false,
      godsKnownDead: { Forge: false, Sun: false, Moon: false },
      ending: "",
      endingText: "",
      completed: false,
      journalTab: "places",
      journalRegion: "north",
      journalSelection: { places: "", notes: "", objects: "" },
      journalReturn: "World Place",
      lastCatMove: -1
    };
  }

  function ensureWorldState() {
    ensureState();
    var v = State.variables;
    if ((!v.world || typeof v.world !== "object") && v.experiment && typeof v.experiment === "object") {
      v.world = clone(v.experiment);
    }
    if (!v.world || typeof v.world !== "object") v.world = freshWorldState();
    var e = v.world;
    if (!e.cat) e.cat = { met: false, adopted: false, name: "the cat" };
    if (!e.places) e.places = {};
    if (!Array.isArray(e.evidence)) e.evidence = [];
    if (!Array.isArray(e.items)) e.items = [];
    if (!e.memories) e.memories = {};
    WORLD_MEMORIES.forEach(function (memory) {
      if (typeof e.memories[memory] !== "boolean") e.memories[memory] = false;
    });
    if (!e.regionVisits) e.regionVisits = {};
    if (!Array.isArray(e.connections)) e.connections = [];
    if (!Array.isArray(e.shrinesSeen)) e.shrinesSeen = [];
    if (!e.journalReturn) e.journalReturn = "World Place";
    if (e.journalTab === "evidence") e.journalTab = "notes";
    if (e.journalTab === "items") e.journalTab = "objects";
    if (["journey", "connections", "notes", "objects", "places"].indexOf(e.journalTab) === -1 || e.journalTab === "journey" || e.journalTab === "connections") e.journalTab = "places";
    if (!e.journalRegion || !worldRegionMeta[e.journalRegion]) e.journalRegion = "north";
    if (!e.journalSelection || typeof e.journalSelection !== "object") e.journalSelection = { places: "", notes: "", objects: "" };
    ["places", "notes", "objects"].forEach(function (section) {
      if (typeof e.journalSelection[section] !== "string") e.journalSelection[section] = "";
    });
    if (!e.academy) e.academy = { nodes: {}, evidence: [], active: "gate", resolved: false };
    if (!e.academy.nodes) e.academy.nodes = {};
    if (!Array.isArray(e.academy.evidence)) e.academy.evidence = [];
    if (!e.commonGround) e.commonGround = { revealed: false, visited: false };
    if (!e.tulip) e.tulip = { found: false, carried: false, leftAtCommonGround: false, destination: "" };
    if (!e.legacyTulipMigrated && v.inventory && Number(v.inventory.tulip) > 0) {
      v.inventory.winterRoot = (v.inventory.winterRoot || 0) + Number(v.inventory.tulip);
      v.inventory.tulip = 0;
      e.legacyTulipMigrated = true;
      e.items.push({
        code: "LEGACY_TULIP",
        name: "Pressed winter root",
        place: "Stalwart",
        description: "A dry red petal remains pressed against the root's pale skin. It crumbles when touched."
      });
    }
    var pressedRoot = e.items.find(function (item) { return item.code === "LEGACY_TULIP"; });
    if (pressedRoot) {
      pressedRoot.name = "Pressed winter root";
      pressedRoot.place = "Stalwart";
      pressedRoot.description = "A dry red petal remains pressed against the root's pale skin. It crumbles when touched.";
    }
    if (!e.godsKnownDead) e.godsKnownDead = { Forge: false, Sun: false, Moon: false };
    if (e.routeBook) {
      var meraBook = e.items.find(function (item) { return item.code === "MERA"; });
      if (!meraBook) {
        meraBook = { code: "MERA", place: "Stalwart" };
        e.items.push(meraBook);
      }
      meraBook.name = "Mera Quill's Route Book";
      meraBook.description = "The inside cover is signed Mera Quill. Four settlements are circled. Beneath them: POSSIBLY ALIVE IS NOT THE SAME AS REACHED.";
    }
    worldShrines.forEach(function (shrine) {
      var permanent = v.storyStatEvents && v.storyStatEvents["shrine_" + shrine.id];
      if (!permanent) return;
      if (e.shrinesSeen.indexOf(shrine.id) === -1) e.shrinesSeen.push(shrine.id);
      if (!e.evidence.some(function (entry) { return entry.code === "SHRINE_" + shrine.id; })) {
        e.evidence.push({
          code: "SHRINE_" + shrine.id,
          region: shrine.regions[0],
          place: "Moonmaiden shrine",
          title: shrine.name,
          text: shrine.text,
          voice: shrine.voice,
          boundary: "A later memorial records a claimed Moonmaiden. It is evidence of memory, not a divine authenticity stamp.",
          countsForRegion: false
        });
      }
    });
    if (!e.pendingEncounter) e.pendingEncounter = null;
    if (v.storyStatEvents) {
      Object.keys(v.storyStatEvents).forEach(function (key) {
        if (key.indexOf("experiment_") === 0 && !v.storyStatEvents["world_" + key.slice(11)]) {
          v.storyStatEvents["world_" + key.slice(11)] = clone(v.storyStatEvents[key]);
        }
      });
    }
    if (!e.version || e.version < WORLD_VERSION) e.version = WORLD_VERSION;
    return e;
  }

  function siteState(code) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (!e.places[code]) {
      e.places[code] = {
        visited: false,
        nodes: {},
        evidence: false,
        danger: false,
        broken: false,
        item: false,
        choice: -1,
        complete: false
      };
    }
    return e.places[code];
  }

  function worldButton(label, handler, disabled) {
    var button = document.createElement("button");
    button.type = "button";
    button.textContent = label;
    button.disabled = Boolean(disabled);
    button.addEventListener("click", handler);
    return button;
  }

  function worldShell(root, site, kicker) {
    root.innerHTML = "";
    var shell = document.createElement("div");
    shell.className = "world-shell";
    shell.innerHTML = '<div class="world-kicker">' + escapeHtml(kicker || worldRegionMeta[site.region].name) +
      '</div><h1 class="world-title">' + escapeHtml(site.name) + '</h1>';
    root.appendChild(shell);
    return shell;
  }

  function addWorldItem(site) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (e.items.some(function (entry) { return entry.code === site.code; })) return false;
    e.items.push({
      code: site.code,
      name: site.item,
      place: site.name,
      description: "Taken from " + site.name + ". Wear, soot, repairs, and handling marks remain where an explanation does not."
    });
    siteState(site.code).item = true;
    notify("Taken: " + site.item);
    return true;
  }

  function addWorldEvidence(site) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (e.evidence.some(function (entry) { return entry.code === site.code; })) return false;
    e.evidence.push({
      code: site.code,
      region: site.region,
      place: site.name,
      title: site.evidence.title,
      text: site.evidence.text,
      voice: site.evidence.voice,
      boundary: site.evidence.boundary
    });
    if (site.minorGod && !e.evidence.some(function (entry) { return entry.code === "MINOR_" + site.code; })) {
      e.evidence.push({
        code: "MINOR_" + site.code,
        region: site.region,
        place: site.name,
        title: site.minorGod.title,
        text: site.minorGod.text,
        voice: site.minorGod.voice,
        boundary: site.minorGod.boundary,
        countsForRegion: false
      });
    }
    if (site.unbrokenClue && !e.evidence.some(function (entry) { return entry.code === "UNBROKEN_" + site.code; })) {
      e.evidence.push({
        code: "UNBROKEN_" + site.code,
        region: site.region,
        place: site.name,
        title: site.unbrokenClue.title,
        text: site.unbrokenClue.text,
        voice: site.unbrokenClue.voice,
        boundary: "This regional tradition preserves one pattern. Alone, it can still describe an unusual human.",
        countsForRegion: false
      });
    }
    if (site.historyFragment && !e.evidence.some(function (entry) { return entry.code === "HISTORY_" + site.code; })) {
      e.evidence.push({
        code: "HISTORY_" + site.code,
        region: site.region,
        place: site.name,
        title: site.historyFragment.title,
        text: site.historyFragment.text,
        voice: site.historyFragment.voice,
        boundary: site.historyFragment.boundary,
        countsForRegion: false
      });
    }
    siteState(site.code).evidence = true;
    notify("Copied into the journal: " + site.evidence.title);
    updateWorldProgress();
    return true;
  }

  function addConnection(key, text) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (e.connections.some(function (entry) { return entry.key === key; })) return;
    e.connections.push({ key: key, text: text });
  }

  function earnMemory(name, reason) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (e.memories[name]) return false;
    e.memories[name] = true;
    e.lastMemoryReason = reason;
    updateSwordStage();
    return true;
  }

  function memoryCount() {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    return WORLD_MEMORIES.filter(function (name) { return e.memories[name]; }).length;
  }

  function updateSwordStage() {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var count = memoryCount();
    var stage = count >= 6 ? 3 : (count >= 4 ? 2 : (count >= 2 ? 1 : 0));
    if (stage <= e.swordStage) return;
    e.swordStage = stage;
    var damage = [3, 4, 5, 6];
    var signs = [
      "",
      "A thin line of silver moves beneath the rust, then is still.",
      "Rust loosens from the blade. The metal underneath is cold and clean.",
      "The old sword rings once in your hand. No one else touched it."
    ];
    State.variables.weapon.name = "old sword";
    State.variables.weapon.baseDamage = Math.max(State.variables.weapon.baseDamage || 2, damage[stage]);
    notify(signs[stage]);
  }

  function regionEvidenceCount(region) {
    return ensureWorldState().evidence.filter(function (entry) { return entry.region === region && entry.countsForRegion !== false; }).length;
  }

  function updateWorldProgress() {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (regionEvidenceCount("holy") >= 2) e.commonGround.revealed = true;
    if (e.places.AN && e.places.AN.choice >= 0 && regionEvidenceCount("central") >= 5) {
      earnMemory("Duty", "Foederati's living rule can be carried, criticized, and corrected by people");
    }
    if (e.places.BN && e.places.BN.choice >= 0 && regionEvidenceCount("desert") >= 4) {
      earnMemory("Future", "Veyra claims a life no dead master can certify");
    }
    if (
      e.places.BF && e.places.BF.evidence && e.places.BF.choice >= 0 &&
      e.places.BG && e.places.BG.evidence && e.places.BG.choice >= 0
    ) {
      earnMemory("Truth", "the council authorization and raw provision ledger prove both the purge and the Demon King's lie");
      addConnection("archives", "Sizzling's guilty record and Boiling's provision ledger are copied into both human and Corrector custody.");
    }
    if (e.places.N && e.places.N.evidence) e.godsKnownDead.Forge = true;
    if (e.places.Q && e.places.Q.evidence) e.godsKnownDead.Sun = true;
    if (e.places.BQ && e.places.BQ.evidence) e.godsKnownDead.Moon = true;
  }

  function worldRegionAt(x, y) {
    var exact = worldSiteList.find(function (site) { return site.coord[0] === x && site.coord[1] === y; });
    if (exact) return exact.region;
    if (y >= 41 && x >= 25) return "demon";
    if (x <= 9 && (y >= 18 || x <= 3)) return "demon";
    if (y >= 42 && x <= 23) return "final";
    if (y >= 35 && x >= 10 && x <= 24) return "inner";
    if (y >= 27 && y <= 35 && x >= 10 && x <= 22) return "outer";
    if (x >= 38 && y >= 18) return "desert";
    if (x >= 36 && y <= 20) return "holy";
    if (y <= 14) return "north";
    return "central";
  }

  var worldEnemyTemplates = {
    oathboundRemnant: { name: "an oathbound remnant", symbol: "§", hp: 48, attackDamage: 7, xp: 30, loot: { medicine: 1, gold: 7 }, attackTimings: { light: [2.7, 3.4], medium: [3.7, 4.5], heavy: [5.0, 5.9] } },
    demonifiedPilgrim: { name: "a demonified pilgrim", symbol: "¶", hp: 56, attackDamage: 8, xp: 36, loot: { moonCharms: 1, gold: 8 }, attackTimings: { light: [2.4, 3.1], medium: [3.3, 4.1], heavy: [4.6, 5.4] } },
    glassJackal: { name: "a glass-backed jackal", symbol: "j", hp: 62, attackDamage: 8, xp: 40, loot: { medicine: 1, gold: 9 }, attackTimings: { light: [2.2, 2.9], medium: [3.0, 3.8], heavy: [4.2, 5.0] } },
    continuityDrone: { name: "a continuity enforcer", symbol: "%", hp: 72, attackDamage: 9, xp: 48, loot: { medicine: 1, gold: 11 }, attackTimings: { light: [1.9, 2.5], medium: [2.7, 3.4], heavy: [3.8, 4.6] } },
    battlefieldEcho: { name: "a battlefield echo", symbol: "†", hp: 78, attackDamage: 10, xp: 54, loot: { medicine: 2, gold: 12 }, attackTimings: { light: [1.8, 2.4], medium: [2.6, 3.2], heavy: [3.6, 4.3] } },
    demandScar: { name: "a living Demand", symbol: "!", hp: 88, attackDamage: 11, xp: 64, loot: { medicine: 2, gold: 14 }, attackTimings: { light: [1.6, 2.2], medium: [2.3, 3.0], heavy: [3.3, 4.0] } },
    stolenEmotion: { name: "a knot of stolen emotion", symbol: "?", hp: 104, attackDamage: 12, xp: 80, loot: { gold: 20 }, attackTimings: { light: [1.4, 2.0], medium: [2.1, 2.7], heavy: [3.0, 3.7] } }
  };

  Object.keys(worldEnemyTemplates).forEach(function (key) {
    var enemy = worldEnemyTemplates[key];
    enemy.victoryText = "The pattern breaks. What remains no longer knows how to repeat the attack.";
    enemy.descriptions = {
      idle: enemy.name + " blocks the path.",
      low: enemy.name + " measures you.",
      mid: "Its next movement begins to take shape.",
      high: "The attack is about to arrive.",
      attack: enemy.name + " attacks.",
      parried: "The Old Sword rejects the heavy blow.",
      dodged: "You leave the light attack nothing to strike.",
      hit: "The attack finds you."
    };
    setup.enemies[key] = enemy;
  });

  setup.enemies.academyDrillEcho = clone(setup.enemies.academyEcho);
  setup.enemies.academyDrillEcho.name = "a training-yard echo";
  setup.enemies.academyDrillEcho.hp = 20;
  setup.enemies.academyDrillEcho.attackDamage = 3;
  setup.enemies.academyDrillEcho.xp = 16;
  setup.enemies.academyDrillEcho.attackTimings = { light: [3.3, 4.1], medium: [4.5, 5.5], heavy: [6.1, 7.1] };
  setup.enemies.academyBreachEcho = clone(setup.enemies.demonHerald);
  setup.enemies.academyBreachEcho.name = "the Academy breach echo";
  setup.enemies.academyBreachEcho.hp = 34;
  setup.enemies.academyBreachEcho.attackDamage = 5;
  setup.enemies.academyBreachEcho.xp = 28;
  setup.enemies.academyBreachEcho.attackTimings = { light: [2.7, 3.4], medium: [3.7, 4.5], heavy: [5.0, 5.9] };

  setup.places = {};
  worldSiteList.forEach(function (site) {
    var town = WORLD_TOWNS.indexOf(site.code) !== -1;
    setup.places[site.code] = {
      code: site.code,
      name: site.name,
      coord: site.coord.slice(),
      passage: "World Place",
      respawnPassage: town ? "World Place" : null,
      modifiers: town ? ["Town"] : (site.kind === "town" ? ["Settlement"] : []),
      exitLine: "The road leaves " + site.name + " behind without making it disappear."
    };
  });
  setup.northernPlaces = setup.places;

  ["central", "holy", "desert", "demon", "outer", "inner", "final"].forEach(function (region) {
    var meta = worldRegionMeta[region];
    setup.regionEvents[region] = {
      weights: { ambient: 58, combat: 30, trader: 7, settlement: 5 },
      ambient: ["scrap", "wanderer", "winterRoot", "snowmelt"],
      combat: [{ type: "single", enemy: meta.enemy }]
    };
  });

  var originalWorldEnterMap = setup.enterMap;
  setup.enterMap = function (key) {
    ensureWorldState();
    var place = setup.places[key] || setup.places.A;
    State.variables.map.region = place.region || worldSitesByCode[place.code].region;
    return originalWorldEnterMap(key);
  };

  var originalWorldMoveMap = setup.moveMap;
  setup.moveMap = function (dx, dy) {
    ensureWorldState();
    var map = State.variables.map;
    var nx = Math.max(1, Math.min(51, map.x + dx));
    var ny = Math.max(1, Math.min(51, map.y + dy));
    map.region = worldRegionAt(nx, ny);
    var result = originalWorldMoveMap(dx, dy);
    map.region = worldRegionAt(map.x, map.y);
    var e = State.variables.world;
    if (e.cat.adopted && map.moves > 0 && map.moves % 7 === 0 && e.lastCatMove !== map.moves && !State.variables.activeMapEvent) {
      e.lastCatMove = map.moves;
      var lines = [
        "The cat steps into your footprint, inspects the road you chose, and follows anyway.",
        "The cat finds shelter from the wind in the exact place your cloak fails to cover.",
        "Something moves beyond the visible road. The cat notices it first and decides it is beneath concern.",
        "You stop to count supplies. The cat counts on being included.",
        "The world is quiet enough to hear four paws and one stubborn pair of boots."
      ];
      setThought(lines[Math.floor(map.moves / 7) % lines.length]);
      setup.renderMap();
    }
    setup.maybeOpenWorldShrine();
    return result;
  };

  setup.maybeOpenWorldShrine = function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var map = State.variables.map;
    if (
      setup.combat ||
      State.variables.activeMapEvent ||
      document.querySelector(".modal-backdrop") ||
      worldSiteList.some(function (site) { return site.coord[0] === map.x && site.coord[1] === map.y; }) ||
      map.moves < 4 ||
      Math.random() >= 0.22
    ) return false;
    var region = worldRegionAt(map.x, map.y);
    var pool = worldShrines.filter(function (shrine) {
      return shrine.regions.indexOf(region) !== -1 && e.shrinesSeen.indexOf(shrine.id) === -1;
    });
    if (!pool.length) return false;
    setup.openWorldShrine(pool[Math.floor(Math.random() * pool.length)]);
    return true;
  };

  setup.openWorldShrine = function (shrine) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (!shrine || e.shrinesSeen.indexOf(shrine.id) !== -1) return false;
    State.variables.storyStatEvents["shrine_" + shrine.id] = { kind: "moonmaidenShrine", shrine: shrine.id };
    e.shrinesSeen.push(shrine.id);
    e.evidence.push({
      code: "SHRINE_" + shrine.id,
      region: shrine.regions[0],
      place: "Moonmaiden shrine",
      title: shrine.name,
      text: shrine.text,
      voice: shrine.voice,
      boundary: "A later memorial records a claimed Moonmaiden. It is evidence of memory, not a divine authenticity stamp.",
      countsForRegion: false
    });
    var backdrop = document.createElement("div");
    backdrop.id = "world-shrine-modal";
    backdrop.className = "modal-backdrop";
    backdrop.innerHTML = '<div class="modal-box" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Moonmaiden shrine"><div class="world-kicker">A statue beside the road</div><div class="modal-title">' +
      escapeHtml(shrine.name) + '</div><div class="modal-text">' + escapeHtml(shrine.text) + '</div><div class="modal-actions"><button class="modal-button" id="world-shrine-offering">Take what was left beneath it</button><button class="modal-button" id="world-shrine-leave">Leave it untouched</button></div></div>';
    document.body.appendChild(backdrop);
    function closeShrine(takeReward) {
      if (takeReward) {
        if (shrine.reward) setup.receiveLoot(shrine.reward, { message: false });
        if (!e.items.some(function (item) { return item.code === "SHRINE_" + shrine.id; })) {
          e.items.push({
            code: "SHRINE_" + shrine.id,
            name: shrine.name + " Offering",
            place: "Moonmaiden shrine",
            description: "A small road-worn offering taken from the hollow beneath the statue."
          });
        }
      }
      backdrop.remove();
      setThought("The statue disappears behind the next rise.");
      setup.updateInventory();
      setup.renderMap();
    }
    backdrop.querySelector("#world-shrine-offering").addEventListener("click", function () { closeShrine(true); });
    backdrop.querySelector("#world-shrine-leave").addEventListener("click", function () { closeShrine(false); });
    return true;
  };

  var originalWorldRenderMap = setup.renderMap;
  setup.renderMap = function () {
    ensureWorldState();
    originalWorldRenderMap();
    var wrap = document.querySelector("#map-wrap");
    if (!wrap) return;
    var old = wrap.querySelector(".world-map-region");
    if (old) old.remove();
    var region = worldRegionAt(State.variables.map.x, State.variables.map.y);
    State.variables.map.region = region;
    var badge = document.createElement("div");
    badge.className = "world-map-region";
    badge.textContent = worldRegionMeta[region].name;
    var pre = wrap.querySelector("#world-map");
    if (pre) wrap.insertBefore(badge, pre);
  };

  function genericNodeAvailability(state) {
    return {
      arrival: true,
      ordinary: Boolean(state.nodes.arrival),
      evidence: Boolean(state.nodes.ordinary),
      danger: Boolean(state.nodes.ordinary),
      broken: Boolean(state.nodes.evidence || state.nodes.danger),
      overlook: Boolean(state.nodes.evidence && state.nodes.danger && state.nodes.broken)
    };
  }

  function genericNodeText(site, node) {
    if (site.code === "A") {
      return {
        arrival: "The outer gate hangs from one hinge. Fresh boot prints pass through it in both directions.",
        ordinary: site.ordinary,
        evidence: "A body lies beside the notice wall. Mud has dried to the courier's boots and coat. A cord beneath the coat holds a small route book closed.",
        danger: "Something scratches beneath the cellar steps. The sound stops when your hand touches the door.",
        broken: "Dead vines cover a ruined trellis. A narrow animal trail passes beneath it.",
        overlook: "From the north wall, the road disappears beneath snow and broken roofs. Several old route markers still face outward."
      }[node];
    }
    if (node === "arrival") {
      return site.kind === "town"
        ? "Boot prints cross older wheel ruts. Smoke finds its way through roofs repaired with three different kinds of wood."
        : "The road gives way to broken stone and a gap wide enough to enter. Wind moves through rooms that once kept it out.";
    }
    if (node === "ordinary") {
      if (site.code === "AW") {
        return ensureWorldState().cat.adopted
          ? "Three cries repeat without changing. The cat ignores them and hisses at a fourth voice farther down the tunnel. The fourth voice coughs."
          : "Three cries repeat at even intervals. A fourth voice farther down the tunnel breaks into a cough.";
      }
      if (site.code === "AY") {
        return ensureWorldState().cat.adopted
          ? "The cat stops before the final road. When you call, it sits and wraps its tail around its feet."
          : "Small paw prints stop at the final road, turn once in place, and lead back the way you came.";
      }
      return site.ordinary;
    }
    if (node === "evidence") return "One corner stayed dry. Something written has been wedged beneath fallen boards and wrapped in what remains of a coat.";
    if (node === "danger") return "Dust trembles from the ceiling. The sound below stops when you stop.";
    if (node === "broken") return "The floor ends at a split running through several rooms. Burned beams point toward a stair on the far side.";
    return "Cold air moves freely here. Below, the paths through the ruin meet and separate without explaining why.";
  }

  function genericRoomName(node, site) {
    if (site && site.code === "A") {
      return {
        arrival: "The outer gate",
        ordinary: "The main square",
        evidence: "The notice wall",
        danger: "The cellar steps",
        broken: "The ruined gardens",
        overlook: "The north wall"
      }[node];
    }
    return {
      arrival: "The threshold",
      ordinary: "The worn rooms",
      evidence: "The dry corner",
      danger: "The lower passage",
      broken: "The split floor",
      overlook: "Open air"
    }[node] || "The ruin";
  }

  function genericRoomPaths(state, node) {
    var paths = {
      arrival: ["ordinary"],
      ordinary: ["arrival", "evidence", "danger"],
      evidence: ["ordinary", "broken"],
      danger: ["ordinary", "broken"],
      broken: ["evidence", "danger"],
      overlook: ["broken"]
    }[node] || ["arrival"];
    if (node === "broken" && genericNodeAvailability(state).overlook) paths.push("overlook");
    return paths;
  }

  function genericPathLabel(state, node, site) {
    if (state.nodes[node] || (node === "danger" && state.danger)) return "Return to " + genericRoomName(node, site).toLowerCase();
    if (site.code === "A") {
      return {
        arrival: "Go back to the outer gate",
        ordinary: "Walk into the main square",
        evidence: "Go to the body by the notice wall",
        danger: "Open the cellar door",
        broken: "Follow the path to the ruined gardens",
        overlook: "Climb the north wall"
      }[node] || "Continue";
    }
    return {
      arrival: "Go back to the entrance",
      ordinary: "Follow the worn passage",
      evidence: "Open the door with writing on it",
      danger: "Go toward the sound below",
      broken: "Cross the collapsed rooms",
      overlook: "Climb toward open air"
    }[node] || "Continue";
  }

  setup.renderWorldPlace = function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var code = State.variables.currentPlaceKey || e.activeSite || "A";
    var site = worldSitesByCode[code] || worldSitesByCode.A;
    e.activeSite = site.code;
    e.regionVisits[site.region] = true;
    var state = siteState(site.code);
    var wasVisited = state.visited;
    state.visited = true;
    var root = document.querySelector("#world-place-root") || passageEl();
    if (!root) return;
    var shell = worldShell(root, site);

    var card = document.createElement("div");
    card.className = "world-card";
    card.innerHTML = '<p>' + escapeHtml(genericNodeText(site, "arrival")) + '</p>';
    shell.appendChild(card);

    var actions = document.createElement("div");
    actions.className = "world-actions";
    if (site.code !== "AZ") {
      actions.appendChild(worldButton(wasVisited ? "Go back inside" : "Enter", function () {
        e.activeMode = "site";
        setup.openWorldNode("arrival");
      }));
    }
    if (site.code === "A") {
      actions.appendChild(worldButton(e.academy.resolved ? "Return to the Academy" : "Take the road to the Academy", function () {
        e.activeMode = "academy";
        setup.openAcademyNode("gate");
      }));
    }
    if (site.region === "holy" && e.commonGround.revealed) {
      actions.appendChild(worldButton("Follow the roots to the Common Ground", function () {
        e.activeMode = "commonGround";
        play("World Room");
      }));
    }
    if (site.code === "AZ") {
      actions.appendChild(worldButton("Walk toward the noise that never stops", function () { setup.openWorldEnding(); }));
    }
    actions.appendChild(worldButton("Return to the world map", function () { setup.enterMap(site.code); }));
    shell.appendChild(actions);
  };

  setup.openWorldNode = function (node) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var site = worldSitesByCode[e.activeSite];
    var state = siteState(site.code);
    var available = genericNodeAvailability(state);
    if (!available[node]) return false;
    e.activeNode = node;
    state.nodes[node] = true;
    if (node === "evidence") {
      addWorldEvidence(site);
      if (site.code === "A") readMeraRouteBook();
    }
    if (node === "broken") state.broken = true;
    if (node === "danger" && !state.danger) {
      setup.beginDungeonCheckpoint();
      e.pendingEncounter = { mode: "site", code: site.code, node: "danger", expectedPassage: "World Room", won: false };
      setup.startCombat(site.enemy, "World Room", { kind: "dungeon", suppressLoot: false });
      return true;
    }
    if (node === "overlook") addWorldItem(site);
    play("World Room");
    return true;
  };

  function resolveSiteChoice(site, index) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var state = siteState(site.code);
    if (state.choice >= 0) return;
    var choice = site.choices[index];
    state.choice = index;
    state.complete = true;
    setup.grantStoryStatExp("world_" + site.code, choice.stat, ({ north: 3, central: 5, holy: 6, desert: 7, demon: 8, outer: 8, inner: 9, final: 10 })[site.region], {
      choice: choice.label,
      message: false
    });
    if (site.code === "AN" && regionEvidenceCount("central") >= 5) earnMemory("Duty", "Foederati's living rule can be carried, criticized, and corrected by people");
    if (site.code === "BN" && regionEvidenceCount("desert") >= 4) earnMemory("Future", "Veyra claims a life no dead master can certify");
    if (site.code === "AT") {
      e.terenTrust = true;
      earnMemory("Trust", "you keep or honestly renegotiate an exact bargain when betrayal would be easier");
      addConnection("teren", "Teren-Seven's exact route models allow human couriers to cross selected demon roads.");
    }
    if (site.code === "B") addConnection("seed", "Byron's spring seed begins moving between Northern, Central, and Desert growers.");
    if (site.code === "AC") addConnection("canal", "Central canal water now reaches Foederati and supplies parts for Traveler's Hope.");
    if (["K", "L", "O"].every(function (code) { return siteState(code).complete; })) addConnection("bells", "The three northern signals answer one another; Sella's lamp is visible beneath them.");
    if (site.code === "BJ") addConnection("pump", "Traveler's Hope pumps water using knowledge gathered across cultures.");
    if (site.code === "BB") addConnection("correctors", "Correctors adopt a revisable leadership compact instead of another permanent strongest ruler.");
    updateWorldProgress();
    play("World Room");
  }

  setup.renderWorldSite = function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (e.activeMode === "academy") return setup.renderWorldAcademy();
    if (e.activeMode === "commonGround") return setup.renderCommonGround();
    var site = worldSitesByCode[e.activeSite] || worldSitesByCode.A;
    var state = siteState(site.code);
    var root = document.querySelector("#world-site-root") || passageEl();
    if (!root) return;
    var node = e.activeNode || "arrival";
    state.nodes[node] = true;
    var shell = worldShell(root, site, worldRegionMeta[site.region].name);
    var room = document.createElement("div");
    room.className = "world-card world-room";
    room.innerHTML = '<h2>' + escapeHtml(genericRoomName(node, site)) + '</h2><p>' + escapeHtml(genericNodeText(site, node)) + '</p>';
    shell.appendChild(room);

    if (node === "evidence" && state.evidence) {
      [site.code, "MINOR_" + site.code, "UNBROKEN_" + site.code, "HISTORY_" + site.code].forEach(function (code) {
        var entry = e.evidence.find(function (candidate) { return candidate.code === code; });
        if (!entry) return;
        var evidence = document.createElement("div");
        evidence.className = "world-evidence";
        evidence.innerHTML = '<h3>' + escapeHtml(entry.title) + '</h3><p>' + escapeHtml(entry.text) + '</p>';
        shell.appendChild(evidence);
      });
    }

    appendSpecialRoomCard(shell, site, node);

    if (node === "overlook") {
      var choiceCard = document.createElement("div");
      choiceCard.className = "world-card";
      choiceCard.innerHTML = '<h3>' + (state.choice >= 0 ? "What you left behind" : "Before you leave") + '</h3>';
      if (state.choice >= 0) {
        choiceCard.innerHTML += '<p>Your work leaves fresh marks among the old ones. The room is quiet when you finish.</p>';
      } else {
        var choiceActions = document.createElement("div");
        choiceActions.className = "world-actions";
        site.choices.forEach(function (choice, index) {
          choiceActions.appendChild(worldButton(choice.label, function () { resolveSiteChoice(site, index); }));
        });
        choiceCard.appendChild(choiceActions);
      }
      shell.appendChild(choiceCard);
    }

    var actions = document.createElement("div");
    actions.className = "world-actions";
    genericRoomPaths(state, node).forEach(function (next) {
      actions.appendChild(worldButton(genericPathLabel(state, next, site), function () { setup.openWorldNode(next); }));
    });
    if (node === "arrival" || node === "overlook") {
      actions.appendChild(worldButton("Step outside", function () { play("World Place"); }));
    }
    shell.appendChild(actions);
  };

  function academyNodeAvailable(node) {
    var academy = ensureWorldState().academy;
    if (node.id === "gate") return true;
    if (node.requiresEvidence && academy.evidence.length < node.requiresEvidence) return false;
    return worldAcademyNodes.some(function (candidate) {
      return academy.nodes[candidate.id] && candidate.next.indexOf(node.id) !== -1;
    });
  }

  function academyPathLabel(academy, node, index) {
    if (academy.nodes[node.id]) return "Return to " + node.name;
    if (node.route === "west") return index ? "Take the farther western doorway" : "Take the western doorway";
    if (node.route === "east") return index ? "Take the farther eastern doorway" : "Take the eastern doorway";
    return index ? "Follow the second open passage" : "Follow the open passage";
  }

  function addAcademyEvidence(key) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (e.academy.evidence.indexOf(key) !== -1) return;
    e.academy.evidence.push(key);
    var def = worldAcademyEvidence[key];
    e.evidence.push({
      code: "ACADEMY_" + key,
      region: "north",
      place: "Northern Academy of Heroes",
      title: def.title,
      text: def.text,
      voice: def.voice,
      boundary: "A roll-call fragment records assignment and response status, not every person's final fate."
    });
    notify("Roll Call fragment recorded.");
  }

  setup.openAcademyNode = function (id) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var node = worldAcademyNodes.find(function (entry) { return entry.id === id; });
    if (!node || !academyNodeAvailable(node)) return false;
    e.academy.active = id;
    e.academy.nodes[id] = true;
    if (node.evidence) addAcademyEvidence(node.evidence);
    if (node.item && !e.items.some(function (item) { return item.name === node.item; })) {
      e.items.push({ code: "ACADEMY_" + id, name: node.item, place: "Northern Academy of Heroes", description: "Dust has settled around the places hands repeatedly missed while using it." });
      notify("Taken: " + node.item);
    }
    if (node.enemy && !e.academy.nodes[id + "_cleared"]) {
      setup.beginDungeonCheckpoint();
      e.pendingEncounter = { mode: "academy", node: id, expectedPassage: "World Room", won: false };
      setup.startCombat(node.enemy, "World Room", { kind: "dungeon" });
      return true;
    }
    play("World Room");
    return true;
  };

  function resolveAcademy() {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (e.academy.resolved) return;
    e.academy.resolved = true;
    setup.grantStoryStatExp("academy_last_drill", "defense", 5, {
      choice: "End Roll Call without inventing a hidden victory",
      message: false
    });
    earnMemory("Limitation", "you cannot make a late arrival successful by discovering a secret rescue");
    addConnection("academy", "Stalwart begins discussing a small school inside the Academy's surviving service court.");
    notify("Thirty-three students. Two staff. Others still unknown. Unknown is not zero.");
    play("World Room");
  }

  setup.renderWorldAcademy = function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var root = document.querySelector("#world-site-root") || passageEl();
    if (!root) return;
    var site = { name: "Northern Academy of Heroes", region: "north" };
    var active = worldAcademyNodes.find(function (node) { return node.id === e.academy.active; }) || worldAcademyNodes[0];
    e.academy.active = active.id;
    e.academy.nodes[active.id] = true;
    var shell = worldShell(root, site, "Northern Region");
    var scene = document.createElement("div");
    scene.className = "world-card world-room";
    scene.innerHTML = '<h2>' + escapeHtml(active.name) + '</h2><p>' + escapeHtml(active.text) + '</p>';
    shell.appendChild(scene);

    if (active.evidence) {
      var evidence = worldAcademyEvidence[active.evidence];
      var found = document.createElement("div");
      found.className = "world-evidence";
      found.innerHTML = '<h3>' + escapeHtml(evidence.title) + '</h3><p>' + escapeHtml(evidence.text) + '</p>';
      shell.appendChild(found);
    }

    if (active.id === "overlook") {
      var resolution = document.createElement("div");
      resolution.className = "world-card";
      resolution.innerHTML = '<h3>' + (e.academy.resolved ? "The last line" : "The loose pages") + '</h3><p>' +
        (e.academy.resolved
          ? "Thirty-three students. Two staff. Others still unknown. Unknown is not zero."
          : "Four pieces of the same roll lie across your knees. Several names end without a mark beside them.") + '</p>';
      if (!e.academy.resolved) resolution.appendChild(worldButton("Write only what the pages support", resolveAcademy));
      shell.appendChild(resolution);
    }

    var actions = document.createElement("div");
    actions.className = "world-actions";
    var activeCleared = !active.enemy || e.academy.nodes[active.id + "_cleared"];
    if (!activeCleared) {
      actions.appendChild(worldButton("Face what remains", function () { setup.openAcademyNode(active.id); }));
    } else {
      var forward = active.next.map(function (id) { return worldAcademyNodes.find(function (node) { return node.id === id; }); })
        .filter(function (node) { return node && academyNodeAvailable(node); });
      var backward = worldAcademyNodes.filter(function (node) {
        return e.academy.nodes[node.id] && node.next.indexOf(active.id) !== -1;
      });
      forward.concat(backward).filter(function (node, index, list) {
        return list.findIndex(function (other) { return other.id === node.id; }) === index;
      }).forEach(function (node, index) {
        actions.appendChild(worldButton(academyPathLabel(e.academy, node, index), function () { setup.openAcademyNode(node.id); }));
      });
    }
    if (active.id === "gate") actions.appendChild(worldButton("Return to Stalwart", function () { play("World Place"); }));
    shell.appendChild(actions);
  };

  setup.renderCommonGround = function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var root = document.querySelector("#world-site-root") || passageEl();
    if (!root) return;
    var site = { name: "The Common Ground", region: "holy" };
    var shell = worldShell(root, site, "Beneath the roots");
    e.commonGround.visited = true;
    var card = document.createElement("div");
    card.className = "world-card";
    card.innerHTML = '<p>Three paths meet around a cold hearth. Small bowls remain where the roots have not lifted them. None bear a crest.</p><h3>' +
      (e.tulip.found ? "The empty patch" : "A flower") + '</h3><p>' + (e.tulip.found
      ? "Dark soil clings to the shape left by the roots. It is warmer than your hand."
      : "A red tulip grows beside the hearth. Everything around it is grey, dry, or dead.") + '</p>';
    if (!e.tulip.found) {
      var tulipActions = document.createElement("div");
      tulipActions.className = "world-actions";
      tulipActions.appendChild(worldButton("Lift it with its living soil", function () {
        e.tulip.found = true;
        e.tulip.carried = true;
        earnMemory("Care", "the world asks for help without guaranteeing what help can accomplish");
        addConnection("magic", "Sella's failed lamp holds light for a full breath. Across the world, dormant Asker instruments twitch toward the living tulip.");
        e.items.push({ code: "TULIP", name: "Tulip with living soil", place: "The Common Ground", description: "Its petals are red. The soil around its roots stays warm inside the cloth." });
        play("World Room");
      }));
      tulipActions.appendChild(worldButton("Leave it rooted until you understand more", function () {
        e.tulip.leftAtCommonGround = true;
        notify("The flower remains beside the hearth.");
        play("World Room");
      }));
      card.appendChild(tulipActions);
    }
    shell.appendChild(card);
    var actions = document.createElement("div");
    actions.className = "world-actions";
    actions.appendChild(worldButton("Return to " + worldSitesByCode[e.activeSite].name, function () { e.activeMode = "site"; play("World Place"); }));
    shell.appendChild(actions);
  };

  function readMeraRouteBook(afterRead) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    e.routeBook = true;
    e.routeChoice = "connect";
    var book = e.items.find(function (item) { return item.code === "MERA"; });
    if (!book) {
      book = { code: "MERA", place: "Stalwart" };
      e.items.push(book);
    }
    book.name = "Mera Quill's Route Book";
    book.description = "The inside cover is signed Mera Quill. Four settlements are circled. Beneath them: POSSIBLY ALIVE IS NOT THE SAME AS REACHED.";
    addConnection("mera", "Mera Quill's unfinished routes join four distant settlements on the same page.");
    notify("The inside cover is signed Mera Quill.");
    if (typeof afterRead === "function") afterRead();
  }

  function appendOpeningWorldHooks() {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var passage = passageEl();
    if (!passage || passage.querySelector(".world-opening-hook")) return;
    if (State.passage === "Stalwart - Main Square") {
      var hook = document.createElement("div");
      hook.className = "world-card world-opening-hook";
      hook.innerHTML = '<div class="world-kicker">Beside the notice wall</div><h3>' +
        (e.routeBook ? "The route book" : "A dead courier") + '</h3><p>' +
        (e.routeBook
          ? "The inside cover is signed Mera Quill. Lord's Rest, Outpost Three, Foederati, and Journeyman's Rest are circled. Beneath them she wrote: POSSIBLY ALIVE IS NOT THE SAME AS REACHED."
          : "Mud has dried to the courier's boots and coat. A cord beneath the coat holds a small route book closed. Four circles show through the rain-stained page.") + '</p>';
      if (!e.routeBook) {
        hook.appendChild(worldButton("Read the route book", function () {
          readMeraRouteBook(appendOpeningWorldHooksRefresh);
        }));
      }
      passage.appendChild(hook);
    }
    if (State.passage === "Stalwart - Ruined Gardens") {
      var catHook = document.createElement("div");
      catHook.className = "world-card world-opening-hook world-cat";
      e.cat.met = true;
      catHook.innerHTML = '<h3>' + (e.cat.adopted ? "The cat" : "A starving cat") + '</h3><p>' +
        (e.cat.adopted
          ? "The cat waits among the dead vines. When you move, it falls in beside you."
          : "A thin cat crouches beneath the ruined trellis. Its ribs show through its coat. It watches the food at your belt.") + '</p>';
      if (!e.cat.adopted) {
        catHook.appendChild(worldButton(State.variables.inventory.food > 0 ? "Feed the cat - 1 food" : "You have no food to spare", function () {
          if (State.variables.inventory.food <= 0) return;
          State.variables.inventory.food -= 1;
          e.cat.adopted = true;
          addConnection("cat", "A starving cat follows after being fed once.");
          setup.updateInventory();
          notify("The cat follows you. It has not supplied a name.");
          appendOpeningWorldHooksRefresh();
        }, State.variables.inventory.food <= 0));
      }
      passage.appendChild(catHook);
    }
  }

  function appendOpeningWorldHooksRefresh() {
    var old = passageEl() && passageEl().querySelector(".world-opening-hook");
    if (old) old.remove();
    appendOpeningWorldHooks();
  }

  function appendSpecialRoomCard(shell, site, node) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (site.code === "A" && node === "broken") {
      var gardenCat = document.createElement("div");
      gardenCat.className = "world-card world-cat";
      e.cat.met = true;
      gardenCat.innerHTML = e.cat.adopted
        ? '<h3>The cat</h3><p>It waits beneath the ruined trellis. When you move toward the gate, it follows.</p>'
        : '<h3>A starving cat</h3><p>It crouches beneath the ruined trellis. Its ribs show through its coat. It watches the food at your belt.</p>';
      if (!e.cat.adopted) {
        gardenCat.appendChild(worldButton(State.variables.inventory.food > 0 ? "Feed the cat - 1 food" : "You have no food to spare", function () {
          if (State.variables.inventory.food <= 0) return;
          State.variables.inventory.food -= 1;
          e.cat.adopted = true;
          addConnection("cat", "A starving cat follows after being fed once.");
          setup.updateInventory();
          notify("The cat follows you. It has not supplied a name.");
          play("World Room");
        }, State.variables.inventory.food <= 0));
      }
      shell.appendChild(gardenCat);
    }
    var unbrokenClueCount = e.evidence.filter(function (entry) { return entry.code.indexOf("UNBROKEN_") === 0; }).length;
    if (site.code === "AU" && node === "ordinary" && e.terenTrust && unbrokenClueCount >= 3) {
      var unbroken = document.createElement("div");
      unbroken.className = "world-card";
      unbroken.innerHTML = '<div class="world-kicker">A person among the names</div><h3>The grave keeper</h3><p>' +
        (e.unbrokenSeen
          ? "He finishes a human marker, then a demon one. Both knots have the same number of turns. When you ask how long he has done this, he looks past you and says, 'Long enough to know returning is not the same as repeating.'"
          : "He restores human and demon markers with identical knots. Each marker stands at the same measured distance from the next. He pauses eight breaths between them, every time.") + '</p>';
      if (!e.unbrokenSeen) unbroken.appendChild(worldButton("Ask why he came back", function () {
        e.unbrokenSeen = true;
        notify("'Difficulty does not remove the option. Returning is part of the choice.'");
        play("World Room");
      }));
      shell.appendChild(unbroken);
    } else if (site.code === "AU" && node === "ordinary") {
      var graveKeeper = document.createElement("div");
      graveKeeper.className = "world-card";
      graveKeeper.innerHTML = '<div class="world-kicker">A person among the names</div><h3>The grave keeper</h3><p>He restores human and demon markers with identical knots. Each marker stands at the same measured distance from the next. He pauses eight breaths between them, every time.</p>';
      shell.appendChild(graveKeeper);
    }
    if (site.code === "O" && node === "ordinary" && e.tulip.found) {
      var lamp = document.createElement("div");
      lamp.className = "world-card";
      lamp.innerHTML = '<h3>Sella\'s lamp</h3><p>The failed lamp holds pale light for a full breath. Sella records the duration twice, then laughs hard enough to ruin the third measurement.</p>';
      shell.appendChild(lamp);
    }
    if (WORLD_TOWNS.indexOf(site.code) !== -1 && node === "ordinary") {
      var services = document.createElement("div");
      services.className = "world-card";
      services.innerHTML = '<div class="world-kicker">Smoke from repaired roofs</div><h3>Rest and prepare</h3><p>A bed has been cleared near the wall. Food and water are stacked behind a rough counter.</p>';
      var serviceActions = document.createElement("div");
      serviceActions.className = "world-actions";
      serviceActions.appendChild(worldButton("Rest to full health", function () {
        State.variables.player.hp = State.variables.player.maxHp;
        setup.commitTownProgress();
        notify("health restored");
        play("World Room");
      }, State.variables.player.hp >= State.variables.player.maxHp));
      serviceActions.appendChild(worldButton("Buy road food and water - 6 gold", function () {
        if (State.variables.inventory.gold < 6) return;
        State.variables.inventory.gold -= 6;
        State.variables.inventory.food += 3;
        State.variables.inventory.water += 3;
        setup.updateInventory();
        notify("road supplies packed");
        play("World Room");
      }, State.variables.inventory.gold < 6));
      services.appendChild(serviceActions);
      shell.appendChild(services);
    }
  }

  setup.renderWorldJournal = function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var root = document.querySelector("#world-journal-root") || passageEl();
    if (!root) return;
    var site = { name: "Journal", region: "north" };
    var shell = worldShell(root, site, "Pages kept dry inside your coat");
    shell.classList.add("world-journal-shell");

    var tabActions = document.createElement("div");
    tabActions.className = "journal-chapters";
    [
      { key: "places", label: "Places" },
      { key: "notes", label: "Notes" },
      { key: "objects", label: "Objects" }
    ].forEach(function (tab) {
      var tabButton = worldButton(tab.label, function () {
        e.journalTab = tab.key;
        setup.renderWorldJournal();
      });
      tabButton.className = e.journalTab === tab.key ? "is-active" : "";
      tabButton.setAttribute("aria-pressed", e.journalTab === tab.key ? "true" : "false");
      tabActions.appendChild(tabButton);
    });
    shell.appendChild(tabActions);

    function knownPlaceEntries() {
      var roomOrder = ["arrival", "ordinary", "evidence", "danger", "broken", "overlook"];
      var places = worldSiteList.filter(function (entry) {
        return e.places[entry.code] && e.places[entry.code].visited;
      }).map(function (entry) {
        var state = e.places[entry.code];
        var rooms = roomOrder.filter(function (node) {
          return node === "arrival" || (state.nodes && state.nodes[node]);
        }).map(function (node) {
          return { title: genericRoomName(node, entry), text: genericNodeText(entry, node) };
        });
        return {
          key: entry.code,
          region: entry.region,
          title: entry.name,
          kicker: worldRegionMeta[entry.region].name,
          rooms: rooms
        };
      });

      var academyRooms = worldAcademyNodes.filter(function (node) {
        return e.academy.nodes && e.academy.nodes[node.id];
      }).map(function (node) {
        return { title: node.name, text: node.text };
      });
      if (academyRooms.length) {
        var stalwartIndex = places.findIndex(function (entry) { return entry.key === "A"; });
        places.splice(stalwartIndex >= 0 ? stalwartIndex + 1 : places.length, 0, {
          key: "JOURNAL_ACADEMY",
          region: "north",
          title: "Northern Academy of Heroes",
          kicker: worldRegionMeta.north.name,
          rooms: academyRooms
        });
      }

      if (e.commonGround.visited) {
        var commonRooms = [{
          title: "The cold hearth",
          text: "Three paths meet around a cold hearth. Small bowls remain where the roots have not lifted them. None bear a crest."
        }, {
          title: e.tulip.found ? "The empty patch" : "A flower",
          text: e.tulip.found
            ? "Dark soil clings to the shape left by the roots. It is warmer than your hand."
            : "A red tulip grows beside the hearth. Everything around it is grey, dry, or dead."
        }];
        var lastHolyIndex = -1;
        places.forEach(function (entry, index) { if (entry.region === "holy") lastHolyIndex = index; });
        places.splice(lastHolyIndex + 1, 0, {
          key: "JOURNAL_COMMON_GROUND",
          region: "holy",
          title: "The Common Ground",
          kicker: "Beneath the roots",
          rooms: commonRooms
        });
      }
      return places;
    }

    var entries;
    if (e.journalTab === "notes") {
      entries = e.evidence.slice().reverse().map(function (entry, index) {
        return {
          key: "NOTE_" + String(entry.code || (entry.title + "_" + index)),
          title: entry.title,
          kicker: entry.place,
          text: entry.text
        };
      });
    } else if (e.journalTab === "objects") {
      entries = e.items.slice().reverse().map(function (item, index) {
        return {
          key: "OBJECT_" + String(item.code || (item.name + "_" + index)),
          title: item.name,
          kicker: item.place,
          text: item.description
        };
      });
    } else {
      entries = knownPlaceEntries();
    }

    var book = document.createElement("section");
    book.className = "journal-book";
    book.setAttribute("aria-label", e.journalTab.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + e.journalTab.slice(1) + " pages");
    shell.appendChild(book);

    var visibleEntries = entries;
    if (e.journalTab === "places" && entries.length) {
      var discoveredRegions = Object.keys(worldRegionMeta).filter(function (region) {
        return entries.some(function (entry) { return entry.region === region; });
      });
      if (discoveredRegions.indexOf(e.journalRegion) === -1) e.journalRegion = discoveredRegions[0];

      var regionNav = document.createElement("div");
      regionNav.className = "journal-region-nav";
      regionNav.setAttribute("aria-label", "Discovered regions");
      discoveredRegions.forEach(function (region) {
        var regionButton = worldButton(worldRegionMeta[region].name, function () {
          e.journalRegion = region;
          var firstKnownPlace = entries.find(function (entry) { return entry.region === region; });
          e.journalSelection.places = firstKnownPlace ? firstKnownPlace.key : "";
          setup.renderWorldJournal();
        });
        regionButton.className = e.journalRegion === region ? "is-active" : "";
        regionButton.setAttribute("aria-pressed", e.journalRegion === region ? "true" : "false");
        regionNav.appendChild(regionButton);
      });
      book.appendChild(regionNav);
      visibleEntries = entries.filter(function (entry) { return entry.region === e.journalRegion; });
    }

    var selectedKey = e.journalSelection[e.journalTab];
    if (!visibleEntries.some(function (entry) { return entry.key === selectedKey; })) {
      selectedKey = visibleEntries.length ? visibleEntries[0].key : "";
      e.journalSelection[e.journalTab] = selectedKey;
    }
    var selectedIndex = visibleEntries.findIndex(function (entry) { return entry.key === selectedKey; });
    var selectedEntry = selectedIndex >= 0 ? visibleEntries[selectedIndex] : null;

    if (visibleEntries.length) {
      var picker = document.createElement("div");
      picker.className = "journal-picker";
      var pickerLabel = document.createElement("label");
      var pickerId = "journal-entry-picker";
      pickerLabel.htmlFor = pickerId;
      pickerLabel.textContent = e.journalTab === "places" ? "Known place" : (e.journalTab === "notes" ? "Copied note" : "Carried object");
      var pickerSelect = document.createElement("select");
      pickerSelect.id = pickerId;
      pickerSelect.setAttribute("aria-label", pickerLabel.textContent);
      visibleEntries.forEach(function (entry) {
        var option = document.createElement("option");
        option.value = entry.key;
        option.textContent = entry.title;
        option.selected = entry.key === selectedKey;
        pickerSelect.appendChild(option);
      });
      pickerSelect.addEventListener("change", function () {
        e.journalSelection[e.journalTab] = pickerSelect.value;
        setup.renderWorldJournal();
      });
      picker.appendChild(pickerLabel);
      picker.appendChild(pickerSelect);
      book.appendChild(picker);
    }

    var page = document.createElement("article");
    page.className = "journal-page";
    page.setAttribute("aria-live", "polite");
    if (!selectedEntry) {
      var emptyMessage = e.journalTab === "places"
        ? "No place names have been written yet."
        : (e.journalTab === "notes" ? "The pages are blank." : "Nothing has been tucked between these pages.");
      page.innerHTML = '<p>' + escapeHtml(emptyMessage) + '</p>';
    } else {
      page.innerHTML = '<div class="world-kicker">' + escapeHtml(selectedEntry.kicker) + '</div><h2>' + escapeHtml(selectedEntry.title) + '</h2>';
      if (e.journalTab === "places") {
        selectedEntry.rooms.forEach(function (room) {
          var section = document.createElement("section");
          section.className = "journal-page-section";
          section.innerHTML = '<h3>' + escapeHtml(room.title) + '</h3><p>' + escapeHtml(room.text) + '</p>';
          page.appendChild(section);
        });
      } else {
        var copy = document.createElement("p");
        copy.textContent = selectedEntry.text;
        page.appendChild(copy);
      }
    }
    book.appendChild(page);

    if (selectedEntry) {
      var pagination = document.createElement("div");
      pagination.className = "journal-pagination";
      pagination.setAttribute("aria-label", "Turn journal pages");
      pagination.appendChild(worldButton("\u2190 Previous page", function () {
        if (selectedIndex <= 0) return;
        e.journalSelection[e.journalTab] = visibleEntries[selectedIndex - 1].key;
        setup.renderWorldJournal();
      }, selectedIndex <= 0));
      pagination.appendChild(worldButton("Next page \u2192", function () {
        if (selectedIndex < 0 || selectedIndex >= visibleEntries.length - 1) return;
        e.journalSelection[e.journalTab] = visibleEntries[selectedIndex + 1].key;
        setup.renderWorldJournal();
      }, selectedIndex < 0 || selectedIndex >= visibleEntries.length - 1));
      book.appendChild(pagination);
    }

    var actions = document.createElement("div");
    actions.className = "world-actions";
    actions.appendChild(worldButton("Close the journal", function () {
      var destination = e.journalReturn && e.journalReturn !== "Journal" ? e.journalReturn : "World Place";
      play(destination);
    }));
    shell.appendChild(actions);
  };

  setup.openWorldEnding = function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    e.activeSite = "AZ";
    if (!siteState("AZ").danger) {
      setup.beginDungeonCheckpoint();
      e.pendingEncounter = { mode: "fear", code: "AZ", expectedPassage: "The Fear", won: false };
      setup.startCombat("stolenEmotion", "The Fear", { kind: "dungeon", suppressLoot: true });
      return;
    }
    play("The Fear");
  };

  function finishWorldEnding(key, title, text) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    e.ending = key;
    e.endingText = text;
    e.completed = true;
    e.endingPhase = "complete";
    State.variables.gameWon = true;
    play("The Fear");
  }

  function resolveTulipDestination(destination) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    e.tulip.destination = destination;
    e.tulip.carried = false;
    if (destination === "fear") {
      finishWorldEnding("world_relearns", "The World Relearns to Answer",
        "You press the warm soil into a crack at the center of the scar. The tulip bends toward the black stone. Days later, Sella's lamp holds light through the night. Wells lift water without rope, then stop, then answer again. New red shoots appear along the old roads.");
    } else if (destination === "common") {
      finishWorldEnding("common_ground", "A Shared Beginning",
        "You return the tulip to the cold hearth beneath the roots. By spring, red flowers grow beside three paths. Couriers carry their seeds along Mera's inked routes. Water rises, signals cross impossible distances, and broken roofs hold long enough for waiting hands to finish them.");
    } else if (destination === "stalwart") {
      finishWorldEnding("small_garden", "The Stalwart Garden",
        "You plant the tulip beneath Stalwart's ruined trellis. Sella's lamp lights. Children clear the Academy's service court and carry slates through its gate. Years later, travelers leave Stalwart with red seeds tied beside their food and water.");
    } else {
      finishWorldEnding("carried_future", "The Unfinished Road",
        "You wrap the tulip's roots and carry it beyond the last mark in Mera's book. Some nights it closes. Some mornings it opens toward a road that was not there before. The cat walks ahead until the grass hides its paws.");
    }
  }

  setup.resolveBrotherPassing = function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    e.endingPhase = "tulip";
    addConnection("brothers", "The Hero passes peacefully after his brother releases the belief that endless battle is the only faithful form of love.");
    play("The Fear");
  };

  setup.renderWorldEnding = function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var root = document.querySelector("#world-ending-root") || passageEl();
    if (!root) return;
    var site = { name: e.completed ? "After the Final Battle" : "The Fear", region: "final" };
    var shell = worldShell(root, site, e.completed ? "What followed" : "Beyond the last road");

    if (e.completed) {
      var complete = document.createElement("div");
      complete.className = "world-card world-ending-choice";
      var endingTitles = {
        world_relearns: "The World Relearns to Answer",
        common_ground: "A Shared Beginning",
        small_garden: "The Stalwart Garden",
        carried_future: "The Unfinished Road",
        two_ghosts: "Two Ghosts at the End of the World",
        burdened_release: "A Brother, Still Carried",
        moonless_dawn: "Moonless Dawn"
      };
      complete.innerHTML = '<h3>' + escapeHtml(endingTitles[e.ending] || "After the Final Battle") + '</h3><p>' + escapeHtml(e.endingText) + '</p>';
      shell.appendChild(complete);
      if (e.cat.adopted) {
        var cat = document.createElement("div");
        cat.className = "world-card world-cat";
        cat.innerHTML = '<h3>At the Gate</h3><p>The cat is still waiting. It sniffs your boots, circles the old sword once, and starts down the road without looking back.</p>';
        shell.appendChild(cat);
      }
      var completeActions = document.createElement("div");
      completeActions.className = "world-actions";
      completeActions.appendChild(worldButton("Continue exploring", function () { setup.enterMap("AY"); }));
      shell.appendChild(completeActions);
      return;
    }

    if (e.endingPhase === "tulip") {
      var passing = document.createElement("div");
      passing.className = "world-card";
      passing.innerHTML = '<h3>Your brother lowers his sword</h3><p>He remembers cleaning armor beside you, sending soldiers back from the Gate, and making you promise to stay alive. "I thought if I stopped," he says, "every death behind me would become wasted." You tell him what you saw on the road. He laughs once, quietly. Then his hand slips from yours. The old sword rings. Silver light moves from the guard to the point and remains there.</p>';
      shell.appendChild(passing);
      if (e.tulip.found && e.tulip.carried) {
        var flower = document.createElement("div");
        flower.className = "world-card world-ending-choice";
        flower.innerHTML = '<h3>The single tulip</h3><p>Its soil is warm through the cloth. The air around the petals trembles when you uncover them.</p>';
        var flowerActions = document.createElement("div");
        flowerActions.className = "world-actions";
        flowerActions.appendChild(worldButton("Plant it in the Fear's scar", function () { resolveTulipDestination("fear"); }));
        flowerActions.appendChild(worldButton("Return it to the Common Ground", function () { resolveTulipDestination("common"); }));
        flowerActions.appendChild(worldButton("Plant it in Stalwart's ruined garden", function () { resolveTulipDestination("stalwart"); }));
        flowerActions.appendChild(worldButton("Carry it beyond the known map", function () { resolveTulipDestination("road"); }));
        flower.appendChild(flowerActions);
        shell.appendChild(flower);
      } else {
        var noFlower = document.createElement("div");
        noFlower.className = "world-card";
        noFlower.innerHTML = '<h3>Morning</h3><p>Dawn reaches the Gate. Far behind you, five columns of smoke rise from five living settlements. A courier bell answers another beyond the ridge.</p>';
        noFlower.appendChild(worldButton("Walk back toward the road", function () {
          finishWorldEnding("moonless_dawn", "Moonless Dawn", "Your brother's hand is empty when morning reaches the Gate. Five settlements exchange food, law, craft, and warning. The wells remain low. The road between them does not.");
        }));
        shell.appendChild(noFlower);
      }
      return;
    }

    var count = memoryCount();
    var clash = document.createElement("div");
    clash.className = "world-card";
    clash.innerHTML = '<h3>Your brother</h3><p>The Hero steps through falling ash. A dying king is reflected in his eyes. He sees the old sword in your hand. "Good," he says. "You brought it. We can finish him again."</p>';
    shell.appendChild(clash);

    if (count < 4) {
      var early = document.createElement("div");
      early.className = "world-card world-ending-choice";
      early.innerHTML = '<h3>He offers you his hand</h3><p>Beyond him, the dead king begins to stand again. Your brother does not look away from it.</p>';
      early.appendChild(worldButton("Fight beside him forever", function () {
        finishWorldEnding("two_ghosts", "Two Ghosts at the End of the World", "You take his hand. The king falls. Ash gathers, and he stands again. Years pass outside the scar. Inside it, two brothers raise their swords each time the dead king smiles.");
      }));
      shell.appendChild(early);
    } else if (count < 6) {
      var partial = document.createElement("div");
      partial.className = "world-card world-ending-choice";
      partial.innerHTML = '<h3>He listens</h3><p>You tell him about the people you met. His sword lowers, but his eyes keep returning to the shape moving in the ash.</p>';
      partial.appendChild(worldButton("Take up the watch and let him rest", function () {
        finishWorldEnding("burdened_release", "A Brother, Still Carried", "Your brother closes his eyes. You remain at the scar with the old sword across your knees. Courier bells sometimes call you back to the road. Each time, you return a little later.");
      }));
      shell.appendChild(partial);
    } else {
      var full = document.createElement("div");
      full.className = "world-card world-ending-choice";
      full.innerHTML = '<h3>There is time before the ash moves again</h3><p>Your brother watches your face instead of the dead king. For the first time, he asks where you have been.</p>';
      full.appendChild(worldButton("Tell him what happened on the road", setup.resolveBrotherPassing));
      shell.appendChild(full);
    }
  };

  function resolvePendingWorldEncounter() {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    var pending = e.pendingEncounter;
    if (!pending || !pending.won) return;
    if (pending.mode === "site" && State.passage === "World Room") {
      var state = siteState(pending.code);
      state.danger = true;
      state.nodes.danger = true;
      e.pendingEncounter = null;
    } else if (pending.mode === "academy" && State.passage === "World Room") {
      e.academy.nodes[pending.node + "_cleared"] = true;
      e.pendingEncounter = null;
    } else if (pending.mode === "fear" && State.passage === "The Fear") {
      siteState("AZ").danger = true;
      siteState("AZ").nodes.danger = true;
      e.pendingEncounter = null;
    }
  }

  setup.verifyBuildOnce = function () {
    var required = [
      "enterMap", "enterPlace", "moveMap", "renderMap", "startCombat", "grantStoryStatExp",
      "saveGame", "continueGame", "newGame", "beginDungeonCheckpoint", "requestDefeat", "resolveDefeat",
      "renderWorldPlace", "renderWorldSite", "renderWorldAcademy", "renderWorldJournal",
      "renderWorldEnding", "openWorldNode", "openAcademyNode", "openWorldShrine",
      "cycleTextSpeed", "toggleInstantText", "showEquipmentPage", "wireModalPages",
      "fitCurrentPage", "scheduleViewportLayout", "installViewportLayout", "auditInterfaceLayout"
    ];
    var missing = required.filter(function (name) { return typeof setup[name] !== "function"; });
    var codes = worldSiteList.map(function (site) { return site.code; });
    var coords = worldSiteList.map(function (site) { return site.coord.join(","); });
    var invalidSites = worldSiteList.filter(function (site) {
      return !site.name || !site.purpose || !site.ordinary || !site.evidence || !site.item ||
        !site.choices || site.choices.length !== 2 || !setup.enemies[site.enemy];
    }).map(function (site) { return site.code; });
    var invalidAcademy = worldAcademyNodes.filter(function (node) {
      return node.next.some(function (next) { return !worldAcademyNodes.some(function (candidate) { return candidate.id === next; }); }) ||
        (node.enemy && !setup.enemies[node.enemy]);
    }).map(function (node) { return node.id; });
    var townFailures = WORLD_TOWNS.filter(function (code) {
      var place = setup.places[code];
      return !place || !place.respawnPassage || place.modifiers.indexOf("Town") === -1;
    });
    var combat = setup.verifyFastCombat();
    return {
      ok: missing.length === 0 && codes.length === 69 && new Set(codes).size === 69 && new Set(coords).size === 69 &&
        invalidSites.length === 0 && worldAcademyNodes.length === 18 && invalidAcademy.length === 0 &&
        worldShrines.length === 10 && townFailures.length === 0 && combat.ok,
      build: setup.__afterFinalBattleBuild,
      missingFunctions: missing,
      placeCount: codes.length,
      uniqueCoordinates: new Set(coords).size,
      invalidSites: invalidSites,
      academyNodes: worldAcademyNodes.length,
      academyEvidence: Object.keys(worldAcademyEvidence).length,
      invalidAcademy: invalidAcademy,
      shrineCount: worldShrines.length,
      minorGodFragments: Object.keys(worldMinorGodFragments).length,
      unbrokenClues: Object.keys(worldUnbrokenClues).length,
      townFailures: townFailures,
      combat: combat,
      protectedTruth: {
        purgeArchive: "BF",
        provisionLedger: "BG",
        firstBattleCoordinateInvented: false,
        huntCoordinate: worldSitesByCode.AV.coord.slice()
      }
    };
  };

  setup.verifyBuildThreeTimes = function () {
    return { firstCheck: setup.verifyBuildOnce(), secondCheck: setup.verifyBuildOnce(), thirdCheck: setup.verifyBuildOnce() };
  };

  $(document).on(":storyready", function () {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (e.pendingEncounter && !setup.combat) e.pendingEncounter = null;
    setup.__afterFinalBattleBuild = "v19-discovery-world";
    State.variables.atfbBuild = setup.__afterFinalBattleBuild;
    updateWorldProgress();
    updateSwordStage();
    document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-atfb-build-verification", setup.verifyBuildOnce().ok ? "pass" : "fail");
  });

  var originalWorldRequestDefeat = setup.requestDefeat;
  setup.requestDefeat = function (checkpointType) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    e.pendingEncounter = null;
    return originalWorldRequestDefeat(checkpointType);
  };

  var originalWorldPlay = play;
  play = function (passage) {
    var e = ensureWorldState();
    if (e.pendingEncounter && !setup.combat && passage === e.pendingEncounter.expectedPassage) {
      e.pendingEncounter.won = true;
    }
    return originalWorldPlay(passage);
  };

  var originalWorldTypewriter = setup.startPassageTypewriter;
  setup.startPassageTypewriter = function () {
    if (["World Place", "World Room", "Journal", "The Fear"].indexOf(State.passage) !== -1) return false;
    return originalWorldTypewriter();
  };

  $(document).on(":passagedisplay", function () {
    ensureWorldState();
    resolvePendingWorldEncounter();
    setTimeout(function () {
      if (State.passage === "World Place") setup.renderWorldPlace();
      if (State.passage === "World Room") setup.renderWorldSite();
      if (State.passage === "Journal") setup.renderWorldJournal();
      if (State.passage === "The Fear") setup.renderWorldEnding();
      appendOpeningWorldHooks();
    }, 0);
  });

})();

:: StoryInit
<<run setup.initializeNewGame()>>

:: Welcome
<div class="welcome-title">After the Final Battle</div>

<<link "Continue">>
  <<run setup.continueGame()>>
<</link>>

<<link "New Game">>
  <<run setup.newGame()>>
<</link>>

:: Shelter
<<print $shelterTexts[$shelterBeat]>>

<<if !$lookedCracks>>
[[Cracks]]
<</if>>

<<if !$lookedSword>>
[[Sword]]
<</if>>

<<if !$lookedStaleBread>>
[[Stale Bread]]
<</if>>

<<if $tookStaleBread and $hasSword>>
[[Door]]
<</if>>

:: Cracks
<<if !$lookedCracks>>
  <<set $lookedCracks = true>>
  <<set $shelterBeat += 1>>
<</if>>

There is only one.

A long, jagged line tears down the wall, opening the room to the street outside.

It is too clean to be age. Too straight to be weather.

A sword did this.

Through the crack, Stalwart leans into itself. Its houses are split open. Its roofs are gone. Some doors still hang, which feels more stubborn than useful.

[[Shelter]]

:: Sword
<<if !$lookedSword>>
  <<set $lookedSword = true>>
  <<set $shelterBeat += 1>>
<</if>>

A dull sword hangs on the door. It still glows faintly, silver beneath the rust. Not enough to warm the room. Not enough to keep anything away.

A memory of brighter days.

It still might be useful.

<<if !$hasSword>>
<<link "Take" "Shelter">>
  <<set $hasSword = true>>
  <<set $weapon.name = "old sword">>
  <<set $weapon.baseDamage = 3>>
  <<run setup.notify("old sword taken")>>
<</link>>
<<else>>
[[Shelter]]
<</if>>

:: Stale Bread
<<if !$lookedStaleBread>>
  <<set $lookedStaleBread = true>>
  <<set $shelterBeat += 1>>
<</if>>

The last two loaves of an old batch. An old waterskin sits near them, half empty.

A sign to start scavenging again.

<<if !$tookStaleBread>>
<<link "Take" "Shelter">>
  <<set $inventory.food += 2>>
  <<set $inventory.water += 5>>
  <<set $tookStaleBread = true>>
  <<run setup.notify("supplies packed")>>
<</link>>
<<else>>
Only crumbs remain.

[[Shelter]]
<</if>>

:: Door
The door opens into Stalwart.

Not the Stalwart from maps. Not the shield city. Not the place people used to point to when they wanted to feel safe.

Just Stalwart now.

Snow, stone, and the kind of quiet that checks your pockets.

[[Main Square|Stalwart - Main Square]]

:: Stalwart - Main Square
<<if $pendingTownWakeMessage>>
<<print $pendingTownWakeMessage>>
<<set $pendingTownWakeMessage = "">>

<</if>>

Stalwart's main square is mostly a crater now.

Markets once crowded the city center. Soldiers drilled beside them. Orders were posted, prayers were said, and everyone tried not to notice when the walls moved. Now snow handles most of the public business.

The Moon statue still stands in the middle. Her face is gone, but one stone hand remains.

<<if !$taken.stalwartSquareCharm>>
A cracked Moon charm hangs from her fingers.

<<link "Take the charm" "Stalwart - Main Square">>
  <<run setup.takeItem("crackedMoonCharm", { flag: "stalwartSquareCharm" })>>
<</link>>
<</if>>

<<if $taken.stalwartSquareCharm>>
[[Slum|Stalwart - Slum]]

[[Rich Housing|Stalwart - Rich Housing]]

[[Academy of Heroes|Stalwart - Academy of Heroes]]
<</if>>

[[Exit|Stalwart - Exit]]

:: Stalwart - Slum
The slum sits beneath the old wall.

Wall-menders, cooks, and leather stitchers lived here. Their children learned early that cold could come indoors without using the door.

The houses are small and close together. Most fell inward when the wall went. No grand collapse, just bad roofs losing an argument.

<<if !$taken.stalwartSlumSearched>>
<<link "Search the tenements">>
  <<run setup.searchLoot("stalwartSlumSearched", { staleBread: 1, scrapIronPieces: 1 }, "The floor gives way before the cupboard does. You find something useful in both.", "Stalwart - Slum")>>
<</link>>
<</if>>

[[River|Stalwart - River]]

[[Main Square|Stalwart - Main Square]]

[[Exit|Stalwart - Exit]]

:: Stalwart - Rich Housing
The rich houses kept their walls longer than the rest of Stalwart.

Good stone, wide rooms, private wells, and enough fireplaces to make winter sound like a problem everyone shared equally.

Some families opened those doors during the retreat. Some did not. The empty houses remember both.

<<if !$taken.stalwartRichSearched>>
<<link "Search the houses">>
  <<run setup.searchLoot("stalwartRichSearched", { sealedFoodTin: 1, northernFieldWrap: 1 }, "Someone hid these behind the good wall paneling. Money had its uses after all.", "Stalwart - Rich Housing")>>
<</link>>
<</if>>

[[Ruined Gardens|Stalwart - Ruined Gardens]]

[[Main Square|Stalwart - Main Square]]

[[Exit|Stalwart - Exit]]

:: Stalwart - River
The river cuts through the lower city.

It has not frozen all the way through. Black water moves beneath the white ice, slow and stubborn and alive at an inconvenient depth.

Stalwart was built around the river because walls need water. So do people. The river has outlasted both kinds of planning.

<<if !$taken.stalwartRiverWater>>
<<link "Fill the jar">>
  <<run setup.searchLoot("stalwartRiverWater", { riverJar: 1 }, "Slightly wet. Could still be useful.", "Stalwart - River")>>
<</link>>
<</if>>

[[Slum|Stalwart - Slum]]

[[Ruined Gardens|Stalwart - Ruined Gardens]]

[[Exit|Stalwart - Exit]]

:: Stalwart - Ruined Gardens
The gardens lie behind the old command house.

Commanders walked here when they needed more time before making a decision. The flowers never offered advice, which may have made them the most sensible people in the building.

Now there are only dead stems, snow, and one small life watching from beneath the ruined trellis.

<<if !$taken.stalwartGardenSearched>>
<<link "Search the gardens">>
  <<run setup.searchLoot("stalwartGardenSearched", { winterRoot: 1 }, "The roots have outlived the beds. Something else in the garden watches what you do with the food.", "Stalwart - Ruined Gardens")>>
<</link>>
<</if>>

[[Rich Housing|Stalwart - Rich Housing]]

[[River|Stalwart - River]]

[[Exit|Stalwart - Exit]]

:: Stalwart - Exit
The western wall has been split open.

It is not a gate. Gates are for cities that still get a say in who enters.

This is a wound in the stone, wide enough to leave through.

<<link "Leave Stalwart">>
  <<run setup.enterMap("A")>>
<</link>>

[[Main Square|Stalwart - Main Square]]

